hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20041","(20041) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, that he used to say: If a night disappears from you, even if If you find your arrows in it the next day and you know them, do not eat them."
"20042","(20042) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If you shot the game and it disappeared from you for a night and it died and you found If your arrow is in it, do not eat it."
"20043","(20043) Ubaidah bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: He asked him A man, and he said: I shoot the game and it disappears from me, then I find it after that, and he said to him: Saeed: If I find it, but not There is nothing in it except your arrow, then eat, but if not, then do not eat."
"20044","(20044) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that Adiy bin Hatim said: O Messenger of God, one of us throws stones. The hunter follows his tracks for two or three days, then finds him dead and there are arrows in him. Should I eat? He said: Yes, if he wants, or he said: He can eat if he wants. (Bukhari 5484, Muslim 1531)"
"20045","(20045) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Adiy ibn Hatim, who said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the hunted army, so I should ask for traces after one night? He said: If you find your arrow in it, and you do not eat seven of it, then eat it. (Tirmidhi 1468. Ahmad 4/377)"
"20046","(20046) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Abdullah said: If you throw If a bird falls into the water, do not eat it, for I fear that the water will kill it. And if you shoot a game bird while it is on a mountain and it returns, do not eat it. If you eat it, I fear that it will become ruined."
"20047","(20047) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Hasan: a similar narration."
"20048","(20048) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man shooting game and missing it. He said: If you find him, he did not fall into the water, nor did he fall from a mountain, nor did he eat. Seven of it, so eat."
"20049","(20049) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Uzza, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, about a chicken that was slaughtered and fell. In water he thought he ate it."
"20050","(20050) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you throw it and it falls into water, it does not You may eat it, but if you throw it and it falls back from a mountain, do not eat it."
"20051","(20051) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol, who said: If it falls in water, do not eat it."
"20052","(20052) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: If you throw a game and it falls into water, it does not You may eat, but if it falls from a mountain, do not eat."
"20053","(20053) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak, who said: If you find him, he will not retreat from a mountain, nor will he It exceeds one hundred percent, so you can eat it."
"20054","(20054) Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of al-Qasim; Concerning a man who threw a hunting animal at a mountain, and it fell back until it fell on the ground and was dead. He said: If he knew that he had died from He ate his ashes, and if he doubted that he died from deterioration, he did not eat."
"20055","(20055) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahhab, who said: Ibn Masoud was asked about a man who hit A man cut it into pieces and said: Leave what has fallen and remember what is left and eat it."
"20056","(20056) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: So He struck the game, and one of his limbs disappeared. He did not eat what he had and ate what was left."
"20057","(20057) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: If a man strikes a hunter Then a part of it left what had fallen and ate what remained."
"20058","(20058) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: He leaves As long as it is clear, he may eat what is left, but if he gives it a large amount, let him eat it."
"20059","(20059) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’. Like him"
"20060","(20060) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a member of his body made clear, he would leave what he made clear and remember what he made clear. It remains, and if he rewards it with two, he will eat it."
"20061","(20061) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who struck a wild animal and lost his hand, or a man while he was alive, then he died. He said: He will eat it, but he will not eat what he has shown. Unless he strikes it and cuts it, then it dies immediately. If that happens, then he may eat it all."
"20062","(20062) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who hits a game animal with something, and the thing appears from it, and he bears what is in it. He said: He does not eat what is visible. Of it, and if they fall together, he will eat it."
"20063","(20063) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’, who said: If the game strikes and a limb falls from it, then It means an organ."
"20064","(20064) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Masruq, who was asked about hunting with sickles. He said: It cuts from Antelope and donkeys, and some of it became clear while it was alive. Ibn Umar said: He did not show it while it was alive, so he left it and everything else. That"
"20065","(20065) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, that he said about the sickles that are placed and passed through them and some of them are cut off. He said: Do not eat."
"20066","(20066) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If the game fell on the ropes, it was in them. If the game catches the iron, then eat it. If the iron does not catch it, then if you do not catch it, then do not eat."
"20067","(20067) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, that he hated hunting with sickles, and he said Salem: It's okay."
"20068","(20068) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Adiy ibn Hatim, who said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, on the authority of the hunted animal, and he said: Whatever you catch with its limit, eat, and whatever you catch with its offspring, then it is safe.\n(Bukhari 54751 Muslim 1529)"
"20069","(20069) Abu Bakr told us, he said: I am Abdullah bin Numayr, he said: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Adiy bin Hatim. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, we are a people who throw stones at places of honor, but what is permissible for us? He said: Do not eat what you have been afflicted with, except what you have slaughtered. (Ahmad 257. Tabarani 162)"
"20070","(20070) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Hudhayfah, that He used to eat what he killed."
"20071","(20071) Ali bin Hashim and Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab He said: Salman said: Whatever is broken, eat it."
"20072","(20072) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Do not eat what has become infected. Turn away unless he is stabbed."
"20073","(20073) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ash`ath, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, the same."
"20074","(20074) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, who said: Makhul narrated to us, that a man came Fadalah bin Ubaid, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with birds that he captured in a shelter, and some of them he put in And some of them he put in a thread, and he said: This is what I have captured with a trace, some of them I have captured His remembrance, and some of them I have not. He said: “Whatever you attain its slaughter, eat it, and if you do not attain its slaughter, do not eat it.”"
"20075","(20075) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah, on the authority of Makhoul, that Fadalah bin Ubaid and Aba Muslim Al-Khawlani used to eat what Al-Ma'arad killed."
"20076","(20076) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Ubaid bin Saad, A man threw a stick at a rabbit and broke its legs, then he slaughtered it and ate it."
"20077","(20077) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Khasif, and he said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about the refusal, and he said: It was not. Of the arrows of the Muslims, do not eat any of it except something that has been crushed."
"20078","(20078) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amer, who said: I asked him about turning away, and he said: If you were correct. With its edge, then it is pierced just as an arrow is pierced, then eat. But if it hits it, then do not eat unless it is slaughtered."
"20079","(20079) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed, that he did not see any harm in what was afflicted. By showing off."
"20080","(20080) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Do not eat what has become ill unless He stabs you."
"20081","(20081) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Do not eat what has fallen upon the sick unless it pricks you."
"20082","(20082) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated what happened to him. Turn away except what is broken."
"20083","(20083) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Qasim and Salem that they were the ones who hated the exhibition. Except as long as His remembrance is attained."
"20084","(20084) Omar bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah bin Ziyad, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: As for Al-Ma’rad, there were people He hated him, he said: He will be punished, but if he is stabbed,"
"20085","(20085) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he did not eat anything. It hit the gun, the stone, and the display."
"20086","(20086) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Sa’id, who said: Ammar said: If you throw a stone or a gun and mention In the name of God, eat, even if he kills."
"20087","(20087) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he did not eat. What happened to the gun and the stone?"
"20088","(20088) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ubad Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of al-Qasim and Salem, that they were in denial. Bundukah except as long as its remembrance is overtaken."
"20089","(20089) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Al-Mughiry, who said: I asked Al-Sha’abi about Al-Ma’rad and Al-Bundaqi, and he said: That is what the people of the Levant give fatwas about, and yet they do not see it."
"20090","(20090) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Do not eat what you have eaten with hazelnuts, unless you slaughter it."
"20091","(20091) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If you are struck by a hazelnut or a stone, do not eat it unless you slaughter it."
"20092","(20092) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: He did not respond to you. He stoned you and ate, and Ikrimah hated it and said: It is a place of refuge."
"20093","(20093) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid: He hated it."
"20094","(20094) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Harmala, who said: Every wild animal you hit with a stick or a stone, Or with a rifle, and I mentioned the name of God upon him, and he took it."
"20095","(20095) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a stone kills you, do not eat."
"20096","(20096) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Do not eat from the hunt of the hazelnut except what I made you smart."
"20097","(20097) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: If a man throws a stone at a hunted animal or a jalajah, it does not You may eat it unless you realize its purity."
"20098","(20098) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The locusts and the nun are intelligent, all of them, so eat them."
"20099","(20099) Ibn Abi Zayd told us, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Zayd, who said: He said: Omar: Whales are all intelligent and locusts are all intelligent."
"20100","(20100) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali said: Locusts and whales are intelligent. All of it, except for what dies at sea, in which case it is death."
"20101","(20101) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hafs, who said: Abdullah said: This is a The whale is the jaw of its beard."
"20102","(20102) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The whale took him away."
"20103","(20103) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, who said: The slaughter of the whale was taken by him. And the locusts are intelligent."
"20104","(20104) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Whatever dies in it, it dies and does not die. You eat"
"20105","(20105) Ibn Aliyah and Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab They hated floating fish."
"20106","(20106) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He did not dislike any of the fish except the floating ones."
"20107","(20107) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’atha’, who said: He hates the taf of water, and eat the carrots."
"20108","(20108) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Hudhayl, he said: A man asked Ibn Abbas, He said: I went to the sea and found it filled with many fish. He said: Eat as long as you do not see floating fish."
"20109","(20109) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father, he said: Ali said: If he dies at sea, it is his death."
"20110","(2010) Abduh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he had a large number of fish. He dies in the water, unless a man takes a pen, but he does not enter it and dies, and he sees no harm in his food."
"20111","(2011) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, in the whale, he is found in The sea is dead, so he forbade it."
"20112","(2012) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, that he disliked the tāfī from it."
"20113","(2013) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he disliked the tawaifiya."
"20114","(2014) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh, that Abu Ayyub found a fish. He floated and ate it."
"20115","(2015) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: I bear witness that Abu Bakr said: Fish floating in water are permissible."
"20116","(2016) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Umar that he did not see fish. The one who floats mightily."
"20117","(2017) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent us with my father. `Ubaidah was on his way, and our provisions ran out, so we passed by a whale that had been thrown into the sea, and we wanted to eat from it, so Abu `Ubaidah forbade us. Then he said: We are the messengers of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and in the way of God, Blessed and Most High, eat, and we ate. He said: When we came to him, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned that to us, and he said: If you have any of it left with you, send it to me.\n(Bukhari 2483. Muslim 17)"
"20118","(2018) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, regarding fish. The water ran away from him, so he said: Eat."
"20119","(2019) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’atha’, who said: Everything that he refrains from."
"20120","(20120) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: He did not abandon the bank of the sea. So eat"
"20121","(20121) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Rabi’i, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Awf said: Whatever comes from the sea is lawful."
"20122","(20122) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Zaid, and Abu Hurairah They said: There is no harm in what was thrown into the sea."
"20123","(20123) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, and it is good that they both said: If the water dries up, then he dies and he sees no harm in eating it."
"20124","(20124) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shar bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, in his saying: {Enjoyment for you And for the sea. He said: The sea does not breathe, even if it is dead."
"20125","(20125) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Humaid bin Sakhr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b al-Qurazi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas in His saying: {Lawful for you is the game and food of the sea} as long as the sea throws a dead person on its back."
"20126","(20126) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: What he said about It appears dead, so it is its food."
"20127","(20127) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: The sea did not speak. It is his food, even if he is dead."
"20128","(20128) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’atha, who said: We were not talking about anything except that his food is salty."
"20129","(20129) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: His food is whatever He slandered"
"20130","(20130) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He did not slander."
"20131","(20131) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, who said: I heard Saeed bin al-Musayyab being asked about sea game. And his food, he said: his food is what he pronounced while it is alive."
"20132","(20132) Hammad bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Saad Al-Jari, he said: I asked Ibn Omar and Ibn Amr about whales dying suddenly, or killing each other, and they said: It is permissible."
"20133","(20133) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he used to hate the whale that She was killed by the whale."
"20134","(20134) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Saad Al-Jari, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, He said: There is no harm in it."
"20135","(20135) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hamid, who said: Abdullah bin Ubaid bin was asked Umar, on the authority of a man who threw his hook and caught a fish, then another fish came and struck it, and half of it went away. He said: He eats what is left."
"20136","(20136) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I said to Burd: A man will be on a mount and stab a donkey and mention the name of God. Or he strikes him with a sword. He mentioned, on the authority of Makhoul, that he said: If he mentions the name of God when he strikes or stabs, then it is not Very bad"
"20137","(20137) Yahya bin Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who stabbed a game animal with his spear and called it poison, saying: He will eat it."
"20138","(20138) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Suwayd, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, who said: He does not eat anything He stabs him in the throat with it, then cuts the veins. He said: This is not slaughter, but killing."
"20139","(20139) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, who said: An antelope would pass by them and they would hit it with their swords. This hand and this man were cut off, so I heard Musaab bin Al-Zubayr giving a sermon and forbidding that."
"20140","(20140) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he hated the hunt of the black dog. Animals"
"20141","(20141) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated it."
"20142","(20142) Abd al-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, that he used to hunt the dog. Al-Aswad and says: He was ordered to be killed, so how can his catch be eaten?"
"20143","(20143) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that he hated the hunt of the black, stingy dog."
"20144","(20144) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas said: What is incapable of you is what is in your hand. In the house of the hunter."
"20145","(20145) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: If any of the camels or cows are scarce, treat it as What are you doing to the beast?"
"20146","(20146) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, about Qurayh that became homeless, he said: It is in the same place as the hunter."
"20147","(20147) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, that a camel raged and a man stabbed it with a spear, so Ali was asked about it. He said: It is all evidence of his incapacity."
"20148","(20148) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim and Al-Shu’bi that they said: When he becomes wild What can be done to a camel or cow?"
"20149","(20149) Abd al-Ala told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan, and on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: He is in the same position as the hunter."
"20150","(20150) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ziyad Ibn Abi Maryam, that a wild donkey became stubborn. On his family, so they beheaded him. Then Ibn Masoud was asked, and he said: That is the quickest slaughter."
"20151","(20151) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: It was A wild donkey was in Abdullah’s house, and a man struck its neck with a sword and mentioned the name of God upon it. Then Ibn Masoud said: It is a hunter, so eat it."
"20152","(20152) Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of something similar, or Like it"
"20153","(20153) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, that a donkey belonged to the family of Abdullah A man struck his neck with a sword, and Abdullah was asked and said: Eat him, but he is a hunter."
"20154","(20154) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, that a bull fought in some of the cities of Medina, and a man struck it. With the sword, and he mentioned the name of God and was asked about it, and he said: It is slaughtered and alive, and he commanded them to eat it."
"20155","(20155) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abaya bin Rifa’ah, on the authority of his grandfather Rafi’ bin Khadij said: We were with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when a camel ran down and a man struck it with a sword. It was mentioned to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Indeed, these animals have creatures like the creatures of wild animals, so whatever of them overcomes you, do with it. This is how\n(Bukhari 2488, Muslim 20)"
"20156","(20156) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan that they saw no harm in his death. Of the fish in the barn."
"20157","(20157) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he had a large number of fish. He dies in the water, unless a man takes a pen, and when he enters it, he dies, not seeing any harm in eating it."
"20158","(20158) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Maqil bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: If you enclose a corral in the water, and whatever dies in it, eat it."
"20159","(20159) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Abaya bin Rifa’a, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said I said: O Messenger of God, we will meet the enemy tomorrow, and we will not have any armor with us. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Hurry, or hurry up. He spilled blood and mentioned the name of God upon him, so eat as long as it is not a tooth or a fingernail, and I will tell you about that. As for the tooth, it is a bone. As for the victory, it is the extent of Ethiopia. (Bukhari 5543, Abu Dawud 2814)"
"20160","(20160) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abu Idris, who said: I saw a man who brought birds, so he called With a sword, they slaughtered them with it."
"20161","(20161) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, he said: Alqamiya was asked about Al-Layta. It will be slaughtered with it and the narwhal, and he said: There is nothing wrong with it, and he said: Everything that breaks the jugulars except the tooth and nail."
"20162","(20162) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim and Al-Shu’bi, who said: There is no harm in slaughtering a lion, or he said: The reed"
"20163","(20163) Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, who said: We discussed something with Abu Al-Sha’atha’. He was reminded of it, and he said: He has not bruised his cheeks, and he has not bruised his cheeks."
"20164","(20164) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whatever swells the veins or sheds blood, everything except the fang and the nail. And the bone."
"20165","(20165) Khaled told us[corrupt] Ibn Hayyan Al-Ruqi, on the authority of Ja’far Ibn Maimun, who said: Everyone who cut the meat and cut the tendons, except that they hated it. Tooth and nail, and they say: They are the extent of the Ethiopians."
"20166","(20166) Omar bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no killing except by assault and hardship, and he did not definite The jugs and the flesh, so everything except the tooth and nail."
"20167","(20167) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Raja’, who said: We went up on Hajj, and a companion of ours caught a rabbit. He did not find anything to remind her of it, so he slaughtered it with a fingernail, and they filled it and ate it, but I refused to eat. He said: Then I met a son. Abbas, so I mentioned that to him, and he said: You did well when you did not eat. He killed her by suffocation."
"20168","(20168) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He should not slaughter with a tooth, a bone, a fingernail, or century"
"20169","(20169) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Murri bin Qatari, on the authority of Adiy bin Hatim, he said: I asked The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of one who is slaughtered with a watertight stick and the two parts of a stick, said: There is no harm in it and he permitted it.\n(Abu Dawud 2817. Ibn Majah 3177)"
"20170","(20170) Abu Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, who said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, on the authority of a male sacrificed animal, and he said: Everything that leaves the anus except a tooth or a fingernail. \n(Muslim 22. An-Nasa’i 4492 AD)"
"20171","(20171) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Abu al-Rabi’, Ibn Abbas was asked about The sacrifice of the reed, if he does not find a knife, and he said: If it breaks and cuts the joints like cutting a knife, and mentions the name of God, then eat. And if you eat a third of it, do not eat. I asked him about the marwa’s sacrifice when he did not find a knife. He said: If it is done, then cut the private parts. So eat, and if you eat a third of it, do not eat."
"20172","(20172) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sayfi, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, brought two rabbits that I had slaughtered in Marwa, so he ordered me to eat them both. (Ibn Majah 3175)"
"20173","(20173) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Safwan, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. (Ahmad, Darami 3, 2014)"
"20174","(20174) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: Sacrifice with your stone, your iron, your promises, and your bones."
"20175","(20175) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Suwayd, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, he said: Everything that causes wounds, And do not eat anything that is soft, and anything that irritates the jugular tissues, so eat it even with a stone or a stone shard."
"20176","(20176) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Sacrifice with stone. And the sword and everything from the blade unless it cuts or bites."
"20177","(20177) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A Bedouin came to the lions and said to him: Slay them. By Marwah? The black man said to him: No, and when the Bedouin stood up, I said: Is there no harm in him slaughtering with the marwa? He said: This man only wants to slaughter his camel, so when it dies, he says: I slaughtered it."
"20178","(20178) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you slaughter with a stick and a stick So you cut your private parts, there is no harm in that."
"20179","(20179) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Salama bin Bishr, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: I asked him about the sacrifice. With the narration, he said: If it is iron and does not return the joints, then eat."
"20180","(20180) Ghandar narrated to us, Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, he said: I heard Al-Shu’abi say: Eat a slaughtered animal. Marwa"
"20181","(20181) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Utba, Ali said: If You will find nothing but marwa, so slaughter with it."
"20182","(20182) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: Everything slaughtered with a blade or a tambourine. And the reed, and the stick, and that which stains the veins and causes blood, and is abhorrent to the tooth, bone, and nail."
"20183","(20183) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, that a boy from Banu Haritha was He was grazing a grain of his own, and death came to it, and he had nothing to remind her of it with. So he took a stake and slaughtered it, so he asked the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Peace be upon him, so he ordered him to eat it."
"20184","(20184) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of Abu Talha Al-Asadi, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas and he came to him. A Bedouin, and he said: I was among sheep, and the wolf spoke, and the ewe plucked from my sheep and scattered its reeds on the ground. So, did you take a handful of sheep? Then I struck some of it against each other until some of it became like a knife, so I slaughtered a sheep with it and shed the blood with it. The veins were cut, and he said: Look at the part of it that touched the earth and cut it off, for it has died, and all of it has died."
"20185","(20185) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, who said: Omar said: Let me prepare for you weapons: spears. And nobility"
"20186","(20186) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Ka’b bin Malik, on the authority of his father, that One of their black female slaves had slaughtered a sheep with a sheep, so he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, and he ordered him to do so. By eating it (Bukhari 2304, Musnad 500)"
"20187","(20187) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: Whatever I concede The jugular is anything but a tooth or a fingernail."
"20188","(20188) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Salama bin Alqamiya, who said: Muhammad was asked about animals slaughtered with a stick, He said: Eat what is not consumed."
"20189","(20189) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The slaughter is in the throat and the pulp."
"20190","(20190) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Asim, that a camel lost its weight. One of those fountains, but they were not able to slaughter it, so they asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and he said: There is no slaughtering machine except one. Ibrahim, peace be upon him."
"20191","(20191) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: We do not slaughter anything except at the slaughterhouse and the slaughterhouse."
"20192","(20192) Yazid bin Harun told us, Hisham Al-Dastawai told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abi Al-Ma’roor, on the authority of Ibn Al-Farafsah: Al-Farafsah was with Omar and ordered him to be called out. Indeed, the sacrifice is in the pulp, and the shaving is for those who are destined and acknowledge it. Souls until they are destroyed. (Abdul Razzaq 8614)"
"20193","(20193) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who slaughtered a sheep, then he ate it from its back."
"20194","(20194) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of a man from Banu Harithah, on the authority of They have a common story: a camel lost its weight, so they asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about it, and he said: stab it and eat it. (Tabarani 4380)"
"20195","(20195) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Siyah, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Masruq, that a camel lost its weight. A well, and its top became the bottom, and Ali said: Cut off its parts and eat it."
"20196","(20196) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab about a camel falling into a well. He said: He shall be stabbed wherever he is destined, and he shall mention the name of God upon him."
"20197","(20197) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashra’, on the authority of his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, what Is it permissible to slaughter anything except in the throat and mandibles? He said: If you had been stabbed in the thigh, I would have rewarded you. (Tirmidhi 1481, Ibn Ajah 3184)"
"20198","(20198) Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Abaya, who said: A camel was riding backwards, and Ibn Umar was present. Then a man came down to slaughter him, and he said: I am not able to slaughter him. So Ibn Umar said: Mention the name of God upon him and let him be rewarded before. He did so, and took out a piece of it, and Ibn Umar took from it ten dirhams, or two dirhams, or four."
"20199","(20199) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of a stolen property in Qarmal that was damaged in A well, and he said: Cut it and eat it."
"20200","(20200) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Siyah, on the authority of Abu Rashid al-Salmani, who said: I was tending to goats. For my family in Dhahir al-Kufa, meaning the tax collector, he said: One of its camels ran away, and I was afraid that he would outsmart me. So she took an iron and placed it in his side, or his hump, then she cut off his limbs and dispersed him among the rest of his family, then I came to my family, but they refused to eat as I told them the news, so I went to Ali and stood at the door of his palace and said: Commander of the Faithful, O Commander of the Faithful, and he said: Labika, Labika, so I told him his story, and he said: Eat. And his infirmity fed me."
"20201","(20201) Mus’ab narrated to us, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, he said: Shurayh and Masruq used to say: Whenever a camel falls into a well and they cannot find a pit for it, let them dig it out with a knife, and it will be slaughtered for it."
"20202","(20202) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of Abu Murra, the client of Aqeel bin Abi Talib, said: I returned to my family, and they had had tea, and lo and behold, he was dead. So I slaughtered it and it moved and went to Abu Hurairah and mentioned that to him and he ordered me to eat it. He said: Then I came. Zayd bin Thabit mentioned her matter to him, and he said: The dead person is moving."
"20203","(20203) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, in The slaughtered animal, he said: If it is struck by its tail, or blinks, or moves, then it is permissible."
"20204","(20204) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father that he had not seen her. It's unfortunate"
"20205","(20205) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you slaughter it, you move a tail, or a limb, or An intelligent man."
"20206","(20206) Abbad told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the sacrifice: If it is slaughtered and moves a limb or leg, then it is slaughtered."
"20207","(20207) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Sabah ibn Thabit, who said: I asked Aamir ibn Abdo about a duck that fell into a well. So they took it out and there was blood in it, and he said: Slay it and eat it."
"20208","(20208) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: If she blinks with her eye, or strikes her tail Or she runs with her foot, then eat."
"20209","(20209) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of al-Dahhak, he said: What I have learned from that is beyond With his eye, or he moves his tail and it is slaughtered, it is permissible. And what was slaughtered and no eye blinked at him, nor did it move. Sin, it is forbidden to die."
"20210","(20210) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Shihab Musa bin Nafi’, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Ali, who said: Sa’id bin Jubayr passed by Ali moved on an ostrich lying on the floor and said: What is this? They said: Are we afraid that you will be detained? He said: You almost called her to Satan, but the real one did not die in his time."
"20211","(20211) Mu’tamar narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Majlis, who said: They used to hope for the suffocating and the suffocating. And the repeated ones, except what you have declared pure. Then God has forbidden all of that, except what you have declared pure."
"20212","(20212) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayd, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, declared sacred the day of Khaybar al-Majthamiyah. (Tirmidhi 1795. Ahmad 2/366)"
"20213","(20213) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade The perched"
"20214","(20214) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: He forbade the roost."
"20215","(20215) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: On the Day of Khaybar, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prohibited the corpse and the secluded person. And the Prophet\n(Tirmidhi 1478. Ahmad 3/323)"
"20216","(20216) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the corpse. (Bukhari 5429. Tirmidhi 1825)"
"20217","(20217) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: What if I shot a rooster, or Did you eat a ram with arrows? He said: No, he is dead."
"20218","(20218) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he used to forbid About that"
"20219","(20219) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, that Ibn Umar passed by a people They set up chickens and threw them at them, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed whoever mutilates animals.\n(Bukhari 5515, Muslim 1549)"
"20220","(20220) Uqba bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Musa bin Muhammad, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: No. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was to be mutilated by animals. (Ibn Majah 3185)"
"20221","(20221) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: People from The Ansar placed doves to throw at them, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the soul from being used as an object.\n(Muslim 1549, Tirmidhi 1475)"
"20222","(20222) Zaid told us, Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Zaid bin Anas, he said: I entered with Anas the emirate’s house. They set up chickens and threw them at them. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the animals to be patient. \n(Bukhari 5513, Muslim 1549)"
"20223","(20223) Abu Al-Muwari’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade And he granted that any animal should be killed with patience. (Muslim 1550, Ibn Majah 3188)"
"20224","(20224) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al Ashaj, on the authority of Ubaid bin Ta’la, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbidding patience. Animals: I do not like that you have given chickens patience, nor that I have such-and-such and such-and-such. (Tabarani 4004, Ahmad 5/442)"
"20225","(20225) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Idris, on the authority of Abu Tha’labiyah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, about eating any of the wildebeest with fangs. (Bukhari 5780 and Muslim 1533)"
"20226","(20226) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd bin Jabir, he said: Al-Qasim and Makhul narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Imamah. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the Day of Khaybar from every wild animal with fangs."
"20227","(20227) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the Day of Khaybar, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade every fanged beast of prey. (Abu Dawud 3799, Tirmidhi 1479)"
"20228","(20228) Hushaym bin Abi Bishr told us, on the authority of Maimun bin Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He forbade every A fang from wild animals, and from every bird with a claw."
"20229","(20229) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama On the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade on the Day of Khaybar every fanged wild animal and every clawed animal. The bird"
"20230","(20230) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awani, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Maymun bin Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade every wild animal with a fang, and every wild animal with a claw. The bird"
"20231","(20231) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: They hated every bird with a claw. And every lion has a fang."
"20232","(20232) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to hate birds that ate carrion."
"20233","(20233) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm in anything that is caught from a bird. And he bit everything with his beak, or took it with his claw, and he hated its own flesh, and he hated the meat of the shrike."
"20234","(20234) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, who said: I said to Mujahid: The Jews do not eat us. Of the birds, except those that were caught. He said: So Mujahid was astonished at that."
"20235","(20235) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Whenever Aisha was asked about Every fanged beast, and every bird with a claw. She said: {I do not find in what has been revealed to me forbidden.} Then she says: The Burmah There will be yellowness in it."
"20236","(20236) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Musa, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, that he disliked eating wild birds and lions. The monster"
"20237","(20237) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: He who eats crow, and the Messenger of God has named him. Is he, may God bless him and grant him peace, a sinner? (Ibn Majah 3248, Bayhaqi 317)"
"20238","(20238) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, who said: I heard Ikrimah being asked about crow and haddya meat. He said: A fat chicken."
"20239","(20239) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he was asked about crow and hadiyya meat, He said: God has permitted what is permissible and forbidden what is forbidden, and He has remained silent about certain things, so whatever He remains silent about, He has pardoned them."
"20240","(20240) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, who said: There is no harm in him."
"20241","(20241) Abbad told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, that he did not see any harm in all birds, unless some of them were dirty."
"20242","(20242) Abbad told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of someone who heard a similar thing to Abraham."
"20243","(20243) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Makin, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: What is not forbidden to you in the Qur’an is yours. halal"
"20244","(20244) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: There is no harm in eating the gerbil."
"20245","(20245) Abdul Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: There is no harm in him."
"20246","(20246) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no harm in the jerboa."
"20247","(20247) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Al-Furat, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Sayegh, on the authority of Ata’, that he said in The wolf cannot be eaten, but the jerboa can."
"20248","(20248) Abdul Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, who said: There is no harm in him."
"20249","(20249) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Wasim, he said: I asked Hassan bin Hussein bin Ali about the jerboa. He said: The wild mouse."
"20250","(20250) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’baa, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about eating jerboa, and they thought about it."
"20251","(20251) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Jubayr bin Shaybah, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Umm A partner, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered her to kill the lizards. (بخاری ۳۳۰۷۔ مسلم ۱۴۲)"
"20252","(20252) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that He ordered that it be killed, meaning the lizard."
"20253","(20253) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far Al-Khutami, he said: My uncle Abdul Rahman narrated to me, on the authority of my grandfather. Uqba bin Fakih said: I went to Zayd bin Thabit in the middle of the day, and I asked him for permission, so he came out girded, with a staff in his hand, and I said: : Where were you at this hour? He said: I was following this animal. God decrees the good by killing it and erases the bad, so kill it. The gecko (Ibn Majah 1316. Ahmad 4/78)"
"20254","(20254) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha that she used to kill the Az-Zaghas."
"20255","(20255) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha that she used to do it."
"20256","(20256) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Amr, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, he said: Who killed And Zaghagha had sincerity with her."
"20257","(20257) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Whoever kills and commits wrongdoing, his sins will be pardoned. Seven sins."
"20258","(20258) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Sa’ib, a client of Fakih bin Al-Mughirah is that she entered upon Aisha and saw a spear placed in her house, and she said: O Mother of the Believers, what are you doing? With this? She said: We kill these lizards with it, for the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told us that Abraham, God’s friend, when He was thrown into the Fire. There was not an animal on earth that did not extinguish the fire other than the lizard, for it used to blow on it. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to be killed. (Ibn Majah 3231. Ahmad 6/109)"
"20259","(20259) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Musa bin Yaqoub, who said: My aunt, my relative bint Abdullah bin Wahhab, she said: Umm Salama used to order the killing of the lizard."
"20260","(20260) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Kill the gecko in the lawful and the sacred."
"20261","(20261) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of his father, who said: Aisha had a cane with which she would kill the gecko."
"20262","(20262) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, that he had ordered the killing of the lizard."
"20263","(20263) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: We were with the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in a cave, and it was revealed to him: {And the messengers according to custom.} He said: So We take them from therein fresh when A snake came upon us, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: Kill her. So we hastened to kill her, but she outran us. By herself, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God protect you from evil just as He has protected you from evil. \n(Bukhari 1830, Muslim 137)"
"20264","(20264) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Omar said: Kill the snakes. All of them in every situation."
"20265","(20265) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umayr, on the authority of Abu Tufayl. On the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, that he used to order the killing of snakes with two fluffs."
"20266","(20266) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Abu Salih, Omar said: Repair your shelters and fear The vermin before they frighten you, for none of them will appear to you safe."
"20267","(20267) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: Whoever kills a living person kills an unbeliever."
"20268","(20268) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: Abdullah said: Kill the snakes. All of them, except for the one who is as if he was filled with water, for he is a jinn."
"20269","(20269) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he used to kill the jinn, and command By killing her and saying: The jinn has transformed the jinn just as apes have transformed the Children of Israel."
"20270","(20270) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Ibn Umar used to order the killing of snakes, then He was ordered to reject us."
"20271","(20271) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: Al-Hasan and Muhammad used to order the killing of snakes, except the jinn. Which is as if it were a silver reed."
"20272","(20272) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to command the killing of snakes, except for the jinn that As if it were a silver bar."
"20273","(20273) Khalaf Ibn Khalifa told us, on the authority of Abu Talha, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: I asked you about killing snakes? He said: I wish I had found someone who would follow them and kill them, and that We would give him a reward for that."
"20274","(20274) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: Killing a living person does not harm any of you. Or he kills an unbeliever, except the one who turns away, then he is a sinner."
"20275","(20275) Abdou told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded He acknowledged the killing of Dhul-Tafateyn, for it seeks sight, and befalls the pregnancy, meaning an evil snake. (Bukhari 3308, Muslim 127)"
"20276","(20276) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi said: Layla: Abu Layla said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about snakes in homes? He said: If you see them in your dwellings, say to them: We urge you to fulfill the covenant that Noah made upon you. We adjure you by the covenant which Sulaiman bin Dawud took from you, that you do not harm us, for if you see any of them So kill them. (Tirmidhi 1485. Abu Dawud 5218)"
"20277","(20277) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Abul-Ayn al-Abdi, On the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever kills a living person kills an infidel.\n(Ahmad 394, Bazzar 1847)"
"20278","(20278) Abu Dawud Al-Hafri Omar bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abd God said: Whoever kills a snake kills an unbeliever."
"20279","(20279) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Whoever kills a living person has killed an enemy. An infidel"
"20280","(20280) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, ordered the killing of dogs. (Ibn Majah 3451. Ahmad 6/143)"
"20281","(20281) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Aban bin Salih, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Salma Umm Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded me in the morning to not leave a dog without I killed him\n(Tahawi 53. Ahmad 6/391)"
"20282","(20282) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet prayed God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded the killing of dogs. We even killed the dog of a woman who brought it from the desert. (Bukhari 3323, Muslim 1200)"
"20283","(20283) Shababih told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, who said: I heard Mutarrif narrating on the authority of Ibn Mughaffal, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the killing of dogs, then he said: What about them and dogs? Then he permitted the hunting dog.\n(Muslim 93 Abu Dawud 75)"
"20284","(20284) Shababi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Asama, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he was depressed. I said: What is the matter with you, O Messenger of God? He said: Gabriel, peace be upon him, promised me that he would come to me, but he did not come to me three days ago. He said: Then a dog passed. Asama said: So I placed My hand was on my head and I became well, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, began to say: What is the matter with you, Asama? So I said: A dog allowed it, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered it to be killed, so it was killed. (Muslim 82. Tabarani 387)"
"20285","(20285) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Uthman ordered the killing of dogs and the slaughter of doves."
"20286","(20286) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, ordered the killing of dogs. Even a woman used to bring a dog in and it would be killed before she left. He said: If it were not for Indeed, dogs are one of the nations. I have ordered them to be killed, so kill every black animal among them that has two dots between its eyes. He is a devil.\n(Muslim 47 Abu Dawud 2840)"
"20287","(20287) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He gave the order to kill the dogs. (Muslim 44. Ahmad 2/113)"
"20288","(20288) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by A donkey was branded in the face, and he said: Didn’t I stop him from doing this? May God curse whoever did this. (Muslim 1060, Abu Dawud 2557)"
"20289","(20289) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade He was blessed to be struck in the face of the animal."
"20290","(20290) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, that he disliked the images being known."
"20291","(20291) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade To multiply the pictures. (Bukhari 5541, Ahmad 2/118)"
"20292","(20292) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God saw me. May God bless him and grant him peace upon a donkey marked between its two eyes. He thought of that and said a strong word about it."
"20293","(20293) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace from hitting him in the face, and from slapping him in the face. (Muslim 106)"
"20294","(20294) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Omar said: He should not be slapped in the face, nor should he be branded."
"20295","(20295) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: He forbade mentioning her in her face."
"20296","(20296) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is disliked for non-Arab women to be branded on their cheeks, or to be slapped. Or dragged by her feet to her altar."
"20297","(20297) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Everything has its sanctity, and the sanctity of animals is their faces."
"20298","(20298) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Othman bin Hakim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Aziz informed me, about Ali bin Murrah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man: “He gave it to me,” or he said, “By his name.” In a sentence, he said: It is for you, O Messenger of God, so he named it the name of truth, then sent with it. (Ahmad 4/173. Tabarani 694)"
"20299","(20299) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: There is no harm in the sky at the back of the ear."
"20300","(20300) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: There is no harm in poisoning the ear."
"20301","(20301) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who said: Ibn Umar passed by my father. And he poisoned and poisoned Qadamah ibn Mad’un, and he said: Ibn Umar: Do not weld, do not weld."
"20302","(20302) Shababa told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Zaid, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik say: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in the sanctuary naming his sheep. I think he said: In her ears.\n(Bukhari 5542, Muslim 109)"
"20303","(20303) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Sulaiman, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked Al-Sha’abi about marking sheep. He called her to her ears, but he saw no harm in it."
"20304","(20304) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, who said: I went with Ibn Umar to Banu Muawiyah and barked. We have dogs. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever keeps a dog, except a ferocious dog, or a livestock animal. Two qirats were reduced from his reward every day. (Bukhari 5480, Muslim 52)"
"20305","(20305) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Whoever keeps a dog, except a hunting dog, or livestock, two qirats will be deducted from his reward each day. (Muslim 51. Ahmad 8)"
"20306","(20306) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever keeps a dog, except a hunting dog, or livestock, his reward will be reduced by two qirats every day. He said: And Salem said: And he said Abu Hurairah: or a plow dog. (Bukhari 5481, Muslim 54)"
"20307","(20307) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who added to it: Or a fearful dog."
"20308","(20308) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Whoever keeps a dog Except for a hunting dog, or livestock, which detracts from its reward of two qirats every day. (Abu Ya’li 5025)"
"20309","(20309) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar ibn al-Walid al-Shinni, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Except for a farming dog, or a hunting dog, or a livestock dog, or a fearful dog."
"20310","(20310) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, who said: Whoever keeps a dog is not a hunting or livestock dog; A decrease in the wages of his household every day by a Qirat."
"20311","(20311) Affan narrated to us, Sulaym bin Hayyan narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: Whoever keeps a dog that is not a farm dog, nor a hunter, nor a livestock dog, will be deprived of his status. His reward every day is one Qirat. (Bukhari 2322. Muslim 58)"
"20312","(20312) Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifi, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, On the authority of Sufyan bin Abi Zuhayr, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Whoever keeps a dog will not be of use. He has no crops and no udder, which detracts from his reward every day by a Qirat. (Bukhari 3325. Muslim 61)"
"20313","(20313) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: Whoever keeps a dog, his reward will be reduced by a qirat every day. (Muslim 50. Tirmidhi 1487)"
"20314","(20314) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: Dogs were permitted in the house of the ma’ūr."
"20315","(20315) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Abi Yazid, on the authority of Abu al-Fadil, who said: Anas used to come with him. He has a dog, so we told him, and he said: He is guarding us."
"20316","(20316) Abdou told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who keeps a dog to guard his house, and he said: There is no good in it except for it to be a hunting dog."
"20317","(20317) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abu Talha, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: The angels do not enter a house in which there are images, or a dog. (Bukhari 3322, Muslim 1665)"
"20318","(20318) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein ibn Waqid, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog. (Ahmad 5/353)"
"20319","(20319) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, he said: Bukair bin Abdullah bin told me. Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zayd bin Khaled, on the authority of Abu Talha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Angels do not enter a house in which there are dogs or pictures. (Bukhari 5958, Muslim 85)"
"20320","(20320) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrak, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Abdullah bin Naja, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog, And no pictures.\n(Abu Dawud 2291, Ahmad 1/83)"
"20321","(20321) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He was loath to shoot his neighbour’s birds, and when He threw it away and paid for it."
"20322","(20322) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, who said: I heard a man asking Nafi’ about hunting pigeons in Medina. He thought about it."
"20323","(20323) Abu Usama told us, or I told on his authority, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he hated the hunting of pigeons. Medina and the cities."
"20324","(20324) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he disliked for a man to be imprisoned, meaning: This one called for this one in his bathroom, and this one called for this one in his bathroom."
"20325","(20325) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Nafi’, that he hated hunting doves in the cities."
"20326","(20326) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, who said: I asked Ibn Abi Layla about a man who attacked a hunter. In Medina, and he said: He will be judged."
"20327","Abu Abdul Rahman told us, Abu Bakr, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shaybah, told us, he said:\n(20327) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abraham’s companions, on the authority of Abraham, on the authority of Mughirah, On the authority of Ibrahim and Al-Sha’bi; Concerning the two partners, they said: The partnership is based on what they agreed upon, and the trust is based on the money."
"20328","(20328) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Jafar, who said: If a man buys goods and shares it with someone, then profit On what they stipulated, and on the money."
"20329","(20329) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim al-Ahwal, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham Abi Kulayb, on the authority of Abraham, regarding the two partners, he brings out: “This is a hundred and this is two hundred.” They said: The profit is according to what they agreed upon. And the one who is in charge of money."
"20330","(20330) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, they said: Profit is based on what they stipulated. And the one who is in charge of money"
"20331","(20331) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The profit is based on what they stipulated, and the bequest is on the head. Money"
"20332","(20332) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, similar to that."
"20333","(20333) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Profit is based on what they stipulated, and the position is based on the share of money. Money"
"20334","(20334) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked al-Hakam, Hammad, and his leaders, about two men. They joined together, one of them brought two thousand, and the other brought a thousand, so they joined together and stipulated that the situation be between them and the profit be between them. Two halves, and he said: The profit is based on what they stipulated, and the deposit is based on the money."
"20335","(20335) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Shurayh, that he said: If a man appoints him as governor by hand With his wife, then another man entered it, so the guarantee is on the owner of the deal and his partner is not owed anything unless it is cash. If it is cash, then the deposit is on the owner of the cash, and the profit is on what they agreed upon."
"20336","(20336) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Ali regarding the mudarib, or the two partners, Sufyan said: I do not know which one he said, profit on what they agreed upon and loss on money."
"20337","(20337) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Husayn, who said: Tawoos was asked, while I was listening, about two partners who joined together. One of them had more capital and was in a better position, so he said: Tawoos: He will not be fined and he has his capital."
"20338","(20338) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, regarding someone who bought something without looking at it in its entirety. Whatever it was, he said: He has the option, if he wants he can take it, and if he wants he can leave it."
"20339","(20339) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
"20340","(20340) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same, and he added: And he has the choice, even if he finds it. As it was stipulated for him."
"20341","(20341) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whoever buys something without seeing it, then he With the option if he sees it, and Muhammad said: If it is as he described, then it is permissible."
"20342","(20342) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, and Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: If he finds it as it was described to him, It is permissible, and he has no choice."
"20343","(20343) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Mahmoul, the client of the Amara family, who said: I was sold to a man. Two Burdens, and I stipulated for him: If he spreads one of them, then it is obligatory. He spreads one of them and it does not please him, so he came to return them both, but I refused. Ali, so I disputed with him to Shurayh, and he said: You are satisfied, but he is not, but the sale is based on mutual consent."
"20344","(20344) Ismail told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Makhoul, who narrated it, saying: If a man buys something, He did not look at it while it was absent from him, so he has the choice. If he looks at it, he can take it if he wants, and if he wants he can leave it. (Daraqutni 8, Bayhaqi 268)"
"20345","(20345) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Harith, he said: If a man buys what is right from the ground, and some of the merchants look at Some of it is obligatory for him if he does not see any defect in what he looks at."
"20346","(20346) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who saw a slave yesterday and bought him today. They said: Not until he sees it on the day he bought it."
"20347","(20347) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Indeed, my father is a man who brings sheep, and he To join a Jew or a Christian. He said: He should not join a Jew, a Christian, or a Magian. He said: I said: Why? He said: Because they usury, and usury is not permissible."
"20348","(20348) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Do not join a Jew or a Christian, and let them not pass by you. In your prayers, if they do so, they are like a dog."
"20349","(20349) Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he did not see any harm in your company. The Jew and the Christian, if the Muslim is the one who is responsible for buying and selling."
"20350","(20350) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman Abi Muhammad al-Naji, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Do not give a non-Muslim person money that is speculated on. And take from it Mudarab money, so if you pass by people who have given it in charity, inform them that it is dhimmi money."
"20351","(20351) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Laith, who said: There was Ata’, a peacock, and Mujahid. They hate your partners, the Jew and the Christian, unless the Muslim is the one in charge of buying and selling."
"20352","(20352) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak, who said: It is not appropriate for a polytheist to participate in tillage. There is no sale that is absent from him, because the polytheist considers usury and the price of a pig permissible in his religion."
"20353","(20353) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah, he said: There is no harm in your company. Jew and Christian if you work with money."
"20354","(20354) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Take from them speculative wealth, and do not You give it to them."
"20355","(20355) Abu Al-Ahwas Salam bin Sulaym told us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to him and said: I lent a man a thousand dirhams for food, so I took half of the loan from him in food, so I sold it for a thousand dirhams, then He came to me and said: Take the rest of your capital: five hundred. Ibn Abbas said: That is what is right, and he has two rewards."
"20356","(20356) Jarir told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, and Ata, who said: Ibn Abbas said that is well-known."
"20357","(20357) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Mutrif al-Asadi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Shurayh that he did not see any harm. To take some of his peace and some of his capital."
"20358","(20358) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyy that he did not see harm in it."
"20359","(20359) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: There is no harm in it."
"20360","(20360) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no problem with him."
"20361","(20361) Abu Saad Muhammad bin Maysar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’tha’i, he said: If he advances a hundred dinars in a thousand severances, there is no harm in him taking five hundred dinars from it and debiting it with fifty dinars."
"20362","(20362) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no problem with him."
"20363","(20363) Waki` narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far bin Burqan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, who said: There is no problem. With it"
"20364","(20364) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Yazid al-Dalani, on the authority of Musa bin Abjar, on the authority of Humaid bin Abd al-Rahman, that A man handed over his dirhams, and he took part of the wheat and part of the dirhams, and he said: There is no problem, that is good."
"20365","(20365) Muhammad bin Maysar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, that Abdullah bin Amr was He was lending him food, so he said to the one to whom he was lending money: Do not take some of our capital and some of our food, but take our capital. Eat it, or eat plenty of food."
"20366","(20366) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I asked him about a man who greets the ladder. So he took some of his dirhams and handed some of his food, so he said: Do not take anything except your capital, or all of it."
"20367","(20367) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
"20368","(20368) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Abu Umar, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: I asked him about it and he said: This is corrupt, no. You take only your capital, or all of your food."
"20369","(20369) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Maqil, about a man who surrendered a hundred dirhams for food. So he took half of his food supplies, and half of them were difficult for him, so he said: No, take your food items, all your capital."
"20370","(20370) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the case of a man who greets him, he takes half of his salam and some of the dirhams he lost."
"20371","(20371) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he used to hate it. To take some of his peace and some of his food."
"20372","(20372) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Bishr, on the authority of those mentioned, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that he was He hated to take some of his peace and some of his wheat."
"20373","(20373) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zayd ibn Jubayr, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: Take the head of your ladder. Or your capital."
"20374","(20374) Abu Dawud Al-Talisi, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Qays bin Saad, on the authority of Mujahid, that: he hated it, And Ata saw no harm in it."
"20375","(20375) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zaid, that he disliked taking some Peace be upon him and some food."
"20376","(20376) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Sawda’, on the authority of Shurayh that he hated it."
"20377","(20377) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr that He hated it"
"20378","(20378) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Salim and Al-Qasim that they disliked that He took some of his peace and some of his food."
"20379","(20379) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Salamah ibn Alqamiya, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he disliked taking some of the Peace be upon him and some food."
"20380","(20380) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Sufyan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, and Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Amr ibn al-Harith ibn Al-Mustaliq and Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, that they disliked for a man to take some of his peace and some of his head. What's wrong with him?"
"20381","(20381) Hafs bin Ghayath and Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bought food from a Jew for a certain period of time, and he showed it to him. Daraa did not mention Ibn Fadil: Until later (Bukhari 2200, Muslim 1226)"
"20382","(20382) Hafs told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no harm in betting in peace."
"20383","(20383) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no harm in taking a bet. In peace"
"20384","(20384) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in a similar manner."
"20385","(20385) Hafs and Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he did not see any harm in betting in peace. He said: Then it was said to him: Saeed bin Jubayr said: That is the guaranteed profit. Abraham said: He may take the mortgage, then it will be withdrawn. Price"
"20386","(20386) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I asked Al-Sha’bi about betting in peace, and he said: I wish I had not I was given nothing except with proof."
"20387","(20387) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab and Ata’ that they were not He sees a strong belief in the mortgage in peace."
"20388","(20388) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid bin Bahram narrated to us, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Asma’ Bint Zaid, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died while his armor was pawned for food from a Jew. (Ibn Majah 2438)"
"20389","(20389) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed away. May God bless him and grant him peace, and his armor was pledged to you for thirty saa’s of barley which he took as a livelihood for his family. (Ahmad 2361 Darmi 2582)"
"20390","(20390) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Dinar, who said: I asked Salim about betting in peace, so he recited (Farhan Maqbool) as if he saw no harm in it."
"20391","(20391) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan Al-Sarraj, who said: I asked Abdullah bin Maqil about a ladder in which a mortgage was taken. Or the tribe? He said: Be confident in what is better for you."
"20392","(20392) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Amir, who said: I am more astonished than he who dislikes the mortgage and the tribe. In peace"
"20393","(20393) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that he did not see any harm in You took confidence in your landlord, and a man said to him: Some people hate the tribe, and they do not see any harm in the sponsor."
"20394","(20394) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Abdullah’s companions did not see him. It's unfortunate"
"20395","(20395) Ibn Abi Zayd told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, like him."
"20396","(20396) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, Salem, and Al-Qasim. They said: There is no problem. By mortgaging in peace."
"20397","(20397) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: If the beginning of it is lawful, then the pledge is of what was commanded. With it"
"20398","(20398) Muhammad bin Fudail told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he was asked about betting in peace. He said: Trust your owner."
"20399","(20399) Malik narrated to us, Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Khaled narrated to us, he said: Amer was asked about betting in peace, and he said: I do not say about it like Ibn Jubayr said: It is a guaranteed usury. (Abdul Razzaq 14092)"
"20400","(20400) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no problem. With the mortgage and the guarantor in peace."
"20401","(20401) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Yazid, on the authority of Abu Iyad, Indeed, Ali hated mortgages and kisses in peace."
"20402","(20402) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais, who said: Ibn Umar was asked about a man who surrenders the ladder and takes the mortgage. He thought about it and said: That is the guaranteed reward, which means profit."
"20403","(20403) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Yazid and Salem, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he used to hate it. The mortgage is in peace."
"20404","(20404) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: Any sale of women is disliked by the tribe. And the bet is on it."
"20405","(20405) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bukair bin Atiq, who said: I said to Saeed bin Jubayr: Should he take the mortgage in peace? He said: That is a guaranteed profit. He said: I said: Should I take the guarantor? He said: That is guaranteed profit."
"20406","(20406) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Shurayh, that he used to hate the mortgage in the Salaf."
"20407","(20407) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, that he hated the Rahn and the tribe. In peace"
"20408","(20408) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Ma’abad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he did not see There is usury between the slave and his master, and he used to sell his fruit to his boys before it was fed."
"20409","(20409) Hafs bin Ghayath, Al-Shaybani, narrated to us on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no usury between the servant and his master; He gives him a dirham and takes two dirhams from him."
"20410","(20410) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Awwam, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It is not between the slave and his master. usury"
"20411","(20411) Ismail told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd On the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no usury between the servant and his master."
"20412","(20412) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I asked Ibrahim and Al-Shu’bi, about a man who had a slave who would provide food. Five dirhams every month, so he said: Give me two hundred dirhams every month, and I will give you nine dirhams every month. He said: He saw no harm in it."
"20413","(20413) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin that they disliked that a man should give He owned the dirhams on the condition that he would increase the yield, and Ibn Sirin said: He would give him a body, or an animal, or something else. That is one of the blessings, and He may add to it whatever He wishes."
"20414","(20414) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd and Al-Hasan, who said: It is not There is usury between the slave and his master."
"20415","(20415) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no usury between the owned and his master."
"20416","(20416) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in selling spices, requiting it after requiting it."
"20417","(20417) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Aamir, who said: There is no harm in selling dates, one part after the two parts, or pieces. After the cut"
"20418","(20418) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Burayd bin Abdullah bin Abi Barda, who said: I asked Ata’ about selling dates. Two parts, he said: It is not valid except two parts."
"20419","(20419) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, that he disliked selling Coconut and henna, and he hates selling cucumbers and bread, except for a pound."
"20420","(20420) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I asked Ikrimah about selling straw, and he said: There is no problem. So I said: It is a spike, so he thought about it."
"20421","(20421) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Omar said: Do not greet chicks until they reach maturity."
"20422","(20422) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: An ear of wheat is not bought until It turns white"
"20423","(20423) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ibn Ash`u and al-Qasim that they disliked selling spices except Thank you very much"
"20424","(20424) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Peace is forbidden in grapes and berries. And dates, and apples, and pears, and melons, and cucumbers, and ears of corn, and dates, and the like."
"20425","(20425) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in a tailor accepting clothes for a known wage. He kisses her without that after he introduces her to something, or he cuts her, or gives her a cloth and needles, and sews There is something in it, but if they do not know about it, or any of it, then they do not take any extra."
"20426","(20426) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad, who said: He did not see any harm in taking the garment. And he gives him two-thirds less than that, and half if he cuts it off, or works on it."
"20427","(20427) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, he said: I asked Ikrimah and Aba al-Aliyah, and I said: A tailor. Should I cut a garment and rent it for less than what I paid for it? They said: Do you do anything with it? I said: Yes, I will cut it and join it. They said: No problem."
"20428","(20428) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad; Concerning a man who gives another man a garment and he rents it to him for less. He said: There is no problem with it if he works on it and cuts it. He said: He seeks his permission. I love you more"
"20429","(20429) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said about the tailor who pays the garment by half, Or a third, or a quarter. He said: If he helps him with something, then there is no problem."
"20430","(20430) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Bayan, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he was asked about the man He buys food and has seen how much it is worth. He says: No, until two saa’s are paid for it."
"20431","(20431) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I told him: I will be watching the food and it will be eaten. Should I buy it for a full price? He said: With every deal like a kilo."
"20432","(20432) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad, the client of the family of Saad, who said: I said to Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: A man bought food. So he bought it, would it be right for me to buy it at a man’s price? He said: No, until it is measured before you."
"20433","(20433) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Khams ibn al-Hasan, on the authority of Maymun al-Qannad, who said: I said to Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab: The man He buys livestock and I look at their weight. Should I buy them by their weight? He said: It used to be said: That is usury, mixed with measure and weight."
"20434","(20434) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abdul Rahman Al-Sulami, who said: A man of great honor came and a man bought it, and he sold it. He was very proud of him, then he wanted to seize her with all of her good thoughts."
"20435","(20435) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Hafs, who said: I heard Al-Hasan, and a man asked him, about a man who bought food, and he was looking at it. To his measure, he said: No, until he measures it."
"20436","(20436) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Sawada ibn Hayyan, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin being asked about two men. One of them bought food and the other had it, and he said: I witnessed the sale and the taking, so he said: Take the profit from me and give it to me? He said: No, not until the two sa's are completed in it, in which case you will have the increase and he will have the decrease."
"20437","(20437) Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, that he was reluctant to buy a garment for a dinar except A dirham of women."
"20438","(20438) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated to buy a garment for a dinar unless A dirham."
"20439","(20439) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, that he disliked buying a garment for a dinar except A dirham."
"20440","(20440) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Sakhr ibn Abi Ghulayth, who said: I saw Abu Salamah Ibn Abdul Rahman bought a dress for a dinar, not a dirham."
"20441","(20441) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no harm in him saying: I sell you for a dinar. And you will give me more dirhams."
"20442","(20442) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Dinar, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Sufyan On the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, that they hated for a man to say to another: I sell you this garment for a dinar minus a dirham."
"20443","(20443) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If a man takes possession of his brother, then he is free."
"20444","(20444) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man owns the property, his paternal uncle, or paternal aunt, or maternal uncle, or her aunt; He is old and in the same position as his parents."
"20445","(20445) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Aban bin Taghlib, on the authority of Talhah, on the authority of Ibrahim and Al-Shu’bi, they said: Who was his uncle’s kingdom? Or his paternal aunt, or his paternal uncle, or his maternal aunt, or any relative of less than that, is a manumitted person."
"20446","(20446) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever has possession of a relative of a mahram, then he is free."
"20447","(20447) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace, likewise. (Tirmidhi 1365, Abu Dawud 3945)"
"20448","(20448) Ali bin Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Omar said: Whoever has the property of a mahram relative, He is free"
"20449","(20449) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of his sheikhs, on the authority of al-Zubayr On the day of Taif, he was owned by his maternal aunts, so he was freed by her ownership of them."
"20450","(20450) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar and Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Al-Mustadawrid bin Al-Ahnaf, who said: A man came to Abdullah and said: My uncle married off his daughter to me and he wants to enslave my son. He said: He does not have it. That"
"20451","(20451) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd and al-Hasan, who said: Who is a merciful king? He is free"
"20452","(20452) Mu’ammar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Not every kin is freed if it is owned by a kin."
"20453","(20453) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: When the paternal uncle, the maternal aunt, and the paternal uncle’s daughter all owned A mahram who was freed."
"20454","(20454) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: No child of his father shall rule, nor a father of his child. He said: And the paternal aunt and maternal aunt are in that position."
"20455","(20455) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: Whoever has a relative’s property, he will be freed, or he will be freed. old"
"20456","(20456) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If the blind or aunt; So that house is yours."
"20457","(20457) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: From the king of a kin; He has been freed, or he is freed."
"20458","(20458) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If the blind And the maternal aunt was freed."
"20459","(20459) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Shu’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, that he used to emancipate the child and the father when The property of one of them is owned by its owner."
"20460","(20460) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The Sunnah has passed that whoever takes possession of a mahram Something, so he is free, with a freed dominion. He said: And beyond that of kinship, God has commanded her connection and forbade her from Its disobedience, and I do not know of anything more disobedient than a man taking his relative as a slave."
"20461","(20461) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a brother owns the property, he will not be freed for him."
"20462","(20462) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: He begins with the deposited."
"20463","(20463) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It begins with trustworthiness."
"20464","(20464) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The depositor, the mudaribah, and the debtor are all in shares."
"20465","(20465) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, Tawus, and Al-Zuhri. They said: They take By rations"
"20466","(20466) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Mudarib and the debtor are the same as long as he does not know anything. With her eyes"
"20467","(20467) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, Abu Ja’far, Ata’ and Al-Zuhri. They said: If he dies He has a debt and has a mudarabah, or a deposit, so they share it in shares."
"20468","(20468) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq and a sinner in debt. The depositary: by shares. Amer said: if they are not found in their own right."
"20469","(20469) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: He reaps the debts."
"20470","(20470) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The deposited person is in the position of the debtor."
"20471","(20471) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Nadr ibn Anas, on the authority of Bashir ibn Nayk, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If a man becomes bankrupt and the man finds his goods standing there, He is more deserving of it than the debtors. (Muslim 1194, Ahmad 347)"
"20472","(20472) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, and Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, that Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith told him, about Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever finds his money with his own money with a bankrupt man, He is more deserving of it than his fines.\n(Bukhari 2402 and Abu Dawud 3513)"
"20473","(20473) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Awf, he said: The letter of Omar bin Abdul Aziz was read to us: Which of the two is a man? If a man became bankrupt and lost his property, then he has more right than all the other fines, unless he borrowed something from his property, in which case he The worst of the fines was decided by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"20474","(20474) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, that he said about a bankrupt person, a man will be found with him. His possessions in his own right. He said: If he took anything from the price of it, then it is the worst of the fines; otherwise, it is his."
"20475","(20475) Hushaym and Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: He is the worst of debtors."
"20476","(20476) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He is the worst of fines."
"20477","(20477) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that a man came to him and said: I paid money to a man He struggled, and set off until he reached Helwan, he died. So I set out and found my bag in his own eyes, and Amer said: You have no choice but to do so. The fines."
"20478","(20478) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Abu Harira, who said: Whoever finds an eye His money is with a man who has gone bankrupt, so he has more right to it than anyone else."
"20479","(20479) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a man becomes bankrupt And your good is the worst of fines."
"20480","(20480) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He is the worst of the fines."
"20481","(20481) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He is the worst of fines."
"20482","(20482) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It is worse, except that it is He has authority to imprison her."
"20483","(20483) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, that Hafsiya bint Omar used Asma bint Zayd as her name. Hujra had her own life. When Hafsah died, Ibn Umar took possession of Hujra."
"20484","(20484) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote that the dwelling Bare. So when he says: “For him and his offspring,” then “it is for him and his offspring.” As long as I remain of them there are women. Then when they all disappear. She returned to her heirs."
"20485","(20485) Ibn Abi Za’idah told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man, the man resides for himself and his descendants, then he dies. He said: His heirs cannot take him out, nor his descendants. One of them remains."
"20486","(20486) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Omar, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, who said: It was Aisha when she was at home. She said: I made you stay at home as long as it seemed to me."
"20487","(20487) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Uthman, my nephew Shurayh, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: Al-Sakini Ali What its owner stipulated."
"20488","(20488) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Uthman, on the authority of Shurayh, something similar."
"20489","(20489) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Al-Shu’bi, who said: Al-Sakini is bare."
"20490","(20490) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about a man who made a man live in his house and he died. The dwelling and the dwelling. He said: It returns to the heirs of the dwelling. He said: I said: O Abu Imran, wasn’t it used to be said: He who owns something? His life, so it is for his heirs after him. He said: That is only in the case of ‘Umri. As for the residence, the wealth, and the bare It will return to her heirs."
"20491","(20491) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If a man gives something and says: It is for you and for your descendants, So it is for him and his heirs. And when he says: Your life is yours, then we will return it to him."
"20492","(20492) Ibn Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: The residence is bare."
"20493","(20493) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: His brothers disputed with Shurayh, and one of them said: He married me off and gave me a home and rewarded me. So he said: Shall I marry him off and give him a home? They said: Marry him in marriage and live with him, and he said: Two just witnesses that he preferred her to himself in his life."
"20494","(20494) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: A man gave a hundred dinars in charity to his son. And they were partners while the money was in the hands of his son. He said: It is not permissible until he takes possession of it. Abu Bakr and Omar ruled: If If he does not feel sad, then there is nothing wrong with him."
"20495","(20495) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Qari, who said: Omar said: What is the matter with men who give their children honey? When one of them dies, he says: My money is in my hand, and if he dies, he says: I have I used to wear it as my son. There is no jewelry except the jewelry in the possession of the child or the parent."
"20496","(20496) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, who said: This was complained to Uthman, that the boy If he was young and did not possess it, then he saw that his father, when he granted it to him and supported him, would possess it."
"20497","(20497) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Uthman, that he said: It is not permissible to tell the truth. Until it is taken away, except for a boy between his parents, then taking them away is a matter of taking possession of it."
"20498","(20498) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I heard Al-Sha’bi say: It is not permissible to give charity until it is received."
"20499","(20499) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, similarly."
"20500","(20500) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: It is not permissible to give charity until it is received."
"20501","(20501) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Mu’adh and Shurayh used to say: It is not permissible to give charity. Until it is taken, except for a boy between his parents."
"20502","(20502) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Nadr ibn Anas, who said: We made him live in half his house. Abu Burda said: If it pleases you to pass it, then take it, for Omar ibn al-Khattab made a decree in Al-Ahal: whatever was taken from him, then it is It is permissible, and unless it is taken from it, it is an inheritance."
"20503","(20503) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad and they said: It is not permissible until he is arrested."
"20504","(20504) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you know the truth, it is permissible, but if you do not hold back, So if he says: My house in such-and-such a place, or my servant, then it is permissible, even if it is not restricted."
"20505","(20505) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Ali, and Abdullah, who said: If you know truthfulness, it is permissible. Even if you do not receive it."
"20506","(20506) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, that Abu Bakr was He gave her a bundle of twenty wasks, and when he came, he said to her: I wish you had saved it, or renewed it, but it was Today is the heir’s property."
"20507","(20507) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Issa bin Al-Musayyab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: If truthfulness is known, it will be accepted or not."
"20508","(20508) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Charity is not permissible until it is received."
"20509","(20509) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Fadil, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is permissible, even if it is not taken."
"20510","(20510) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of the one who told him, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Charity is not permissible until it is received."
"20511","(20511) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He saw no harm. By writing on the descriptions."
"20512","(20512) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, that Hafsiya wrote a servant for her to be appointed to Wasfa’."
"20513","(20513) Hushaym bin Bashir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Siwar, who said: I was told by a circumciser who is called Sarah. A servant of Abu Barzah: Abu Barzah appointed some of his kingdoms to a slave."
"20514","(20514) Hushaym and Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in a slave writing to Ali. The descriptions.\nJarir added to it: And the descriptions."
"20515","(20515) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: There is no harm in a slave writing to Ali Al-Wasfa’i."
"20516","(20516) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin that they did not see any harm in it. The office is written to the successors."
"20517","(20517) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no harm in his servant writing to the Wasfa’is."
"20518","(20518) Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he did not see any harm in The man is written as his property over the successors."
"20519","(20519) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ikrim bin Khalid Al-Makhzoumi, that a man wrote to Abd Ali had two boys who would do something similar to his work. They went to Omar ibn Al-Khattab and said: If he does not bring you two boys who would do something similar to his work. His craftsmanship and his return to slavery."
"20520","(20520) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no harm in his servant writing down a slave for a term. Named"
"20521","(20521) Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul-Aziz, that he was not He sees harm in writing to the successors, hand to hand, and he hates that by women, and that is the view of his followers."
"20522","(20522) Waki’ told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Bakr bin Anas, he said: This Sirin’s letter to us is that this is what Anas bin Malik, his servant, wrote about him. He wrote it down for such-and-such out of a thousand. And Ali has two of his boys who do the same work as him."
"20523","(20523) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: He forbade, on the authority of the evil eye.\n(Bukhari 2126, Muslim 1160)"
"20524","(20524) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The evil eye is forbidden."
"20525","(20525) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah, that he used to view tawarruq as meaning The eye"
"20526","(20526) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he hated the evil eye."
"20527","(20527) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: They mentioned it with Muhammad Al-Aynah, and he said: I was informed, that Ibn Abbas used to say: A dirham for a dirham, and between the two of them was a free animal."
"20528","(20528) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Janab and Yazid bin Mardanaba, one of them said: We came, and the other said: A letter from Omar bin Abdul Aziz came to Abdul Hamid: He who accepted it from you on the authority of the loan, for it is the sister of usury."
"20529","(20529) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of al-Rabi’, on the authority of al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin that they hated the evil eye and did not let people into it. Between her"
"20530","(20530) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard something stolen that was displeasing to the eye. And silk."
"20531","(20531) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hamza Imran bin Abi Ata’, who said: I witnessed Sharih and he concluded a dispute with him. Two men ran away from each other, moving to a known place, and passed by, and a group kept them safe."
"20532","(20532) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, who said: I asked Abraham about a man who attacked an animal. So he went ahead with it and said: He is a guarantor, and there is no blame on him for what he violates."
"20533","(20533) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: When the animal is delivered, two bows of fire gather upon it."
"20534","(20534) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ibn Abi Zayd told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Thaqafi told me, on the authority of An explanation is that it was a case concerning a man who hired an animal from a man to go to Al-Bardamah, and he had passed the time for it and it became damaged and died, so he made a burden on it. The reward goes to the place that has been named, and the animal guarantees it when it violates it."
"20535","(20535) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When a man hides his mount, The place was his possession, but if he passed over it and she spent, he had its first lease, and he must secure it."
"20536","(20536) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Awn, on the authority of Shuraih, about a man who saddled an animal and passed the time. He said: The rent and guarantee are combined."
"20537","(20537) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of the ruling regarding a man who bought something from a man that perished in his hands. The seller, before he took possession of it, said: If he said to him: Take your belongings, and he did not take them, then it is from the buyer’s money. And if it is, he says: I will not pay it to you until you bring the price, then it is the seller’s money."
"20538","(20538) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us on the authority of Dawud, he said: I said to Amir: A man bought fine linen for a certain period of time, so he locked it up, gagged it, and put it in He was at the seller's house and he did not hold him as a collateral for the money, so the money was burned, so he said: From the seller's money."
"20539","(20539) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man buys goods and says: The buyer: Transfer it to me, and the seller said: No, until you bring me the price, for this is the same as the mortgage. If it is lost, it is from the seller’s money. And if the seller says to the buyer: Move it, and he says: Leave it until I bring you the price, then this is in its deposited state, if it is lost to you. So it is from the buyer’s money, and he sells this and does not sell that. Ibn Aoun said: So I mentioned it to Muhammad, and he said: He is right. I think"
"20540","(20540) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, that a man bought goods from another man for a term. And he imprisoned him, and there was a fire in their house during the night, and some of it was burned. I asked Al-Sha’bi and he said: It is from the wealth of the one who had it. His hands"
"20541","(20541) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: If he stipulated that he would not go out, And he does not get married. He said: His condition is invalid. He goes wherever he wants and gets married."
"20542","(20542) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ubaydah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: You stipulate conditions that are not permissible. You stipulate that he neither go out nor get married. He said: He should go out and get married."
"20543","(20543) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, the same."
"20544","(20544) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The people of the offices do not stipulate Upon him and upon them is what they take from him."
"20545","(20545) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Jahm, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, who said: He will leave if he wishes."
"20546","(20546) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a man who stipulated that he would not go out in office. He said: He will come out, Waki’ said, and Sufyan said: He will not go out except with the permission of his master."
"20547","(20547) Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya, who said: My mother told me that her grandfather was Writing to Abdullah bin Qais Al-Aslami, he wanted to go out to Basra, but he prevented him, so Othman came and said: You are not allowed to You prevented him, so he abandoned him."
"20548","(20548) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir; Regarding a man who stipulates that he does not go out or get married, he said: He gets married and goes out."
"20549","(20549) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They hated to stipulate The one who is appointed must not be harmed by: not to leave Egypt, nor to get married."
"20550","(20550) Sharik bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Khabab was a strong man, and he Perhaps he bought a sword decorated with paper, and perhaps he mentioned the Qur’an."
"20551","(20551) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no harm in buying a local sword. In dirhams."
"20552","(20552) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in buying a silver sword with delay."
"20553","(20553) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin that he hated it."
"20554","(20554) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Anas, who said: The letter of Omar came to us while we In the land of Persia, that you do not sell swords containing silver rings for dirhams."
"20555","(20555) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Yazid, who said: I heard Khaled bin Abi Imran speaking, on the authority of Hanash, On the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid, he said: On the day of the news of the news, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was given necklaces with beads strung on them. With gold that a man bought for nine dinars, or for seven, it was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he mentioned that to him. He said: No, until you distinguish what is between them. He said: I only wanted the stones. He said: No, until you distinguish what is between them. He said: He spread it until He distinguished what was between them.\n(Muslim 1214, Abu Dawud 3344)"
"20556","(20556) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Shurayh was asked about a golden bow that had stones in it, and he said: The cloves are removed, then the gold is bought weight for weight."
"20557","(20557) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Jewelry and swords are not sold. Sweetened with women."
"20558","(20558) Othman bin Matar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his commanders that they did not see It is unfortunate to buy a silver sword, a silver bow and a silver cup for dirhams."
"20559","(20559) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, that he used to hate being bought. The sword decorated with silver, and it says: “Bought it with gold, hand in hand.”"
"20560","(20560) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Rahman, who said: I asked Suleiman bin Musa about the local sword. With silver, and he said: There is no problem with it, and Makhoul said: The slave girl is sold while she has jewelry on her."
"20561","(20561) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Sha’bah, he said: I asked Hammad about the local sword that is sold for dirhams, and he said: There is no problem with it. The ruling said: If the dirhams are more than the jewelry, then there is nothing wrong with them."
"20562","(20562) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Ammarah bin Abi Hafsa, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Hunayn, he said: Ali was asked About bowls of gold, mixed with silver, sold for silver? He said: So he said: Thus with his head, there is no harm in it."
"20563","(20563) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, that Muhammad used to dislike buying the local sword unless it was an accident."
"20564","(20564) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he did not see It is unfortunate if the price is more than the jewelry, and it is disliked if the price is less than the jewelry."
"20565","(20565) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba and others, that Al-Hasan was not seen. It is difficult to buy a local sword and a ring with dirhams."
"20566","(20566) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Yazid al-Dalani, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, who said: We used to buy and sell swords decorated with silver."
"20567","(20567) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: No. There is nothing wrong with selling a local sword for dirhams."
"20568","(20568) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no problem. By selling to whomever exceeds, fifths were also sold."
"20569","(20569) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, that he disliked selling to anyone except the partners. Between them."
"20570","(20570) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz sent Umairah bin Yazid The Palestinian was selling the captives to Yazid. When he finished, he came to him and said to him: Omar: How was the sale today? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, if he is negligent, if it were not that I would add more to them and spend on him, then Omar said: I would. Do you give them more money, but do you not want to buy? He said: Yes, Omar said, This dispute is not permissible. O Amira, send a caller to call out, “The sale is rejected, and the dispute is not permissible.”"
"20571","(20571) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hazzam bin Hisham Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of his father, who said: I witnessed Omar bin Al-Khattab selling camels from... The camel of charity is from Yazid."
"20572","(20572) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Akhdar bin Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Hanafi, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, On the authority of a man from the Ansar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sold peas and cup to Yazeed.\n(Nasa’i 6099. Tirmidhi 479)"
"20573","(20573) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, who said: There is no harm in selling to anyone for more, if you increase the price if you want To buy"
"20574","(20574) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin that they disliked selling to anyone except Yazid. Selling inheritance and spoils."
"20575","(20575) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of someone who heard Mujahid and Ata’ saying: There is no harm in selling to someone who has more."
"20576","(20576) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Abu Ja`far Al-Khutmi, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin His people is that he sold the spoils to Yazid."
"20577","(20577) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Muslim bin Subaih, who said: A man came to me from Al-Basra and he had copies of the Qur’an that he was selling, so I went to Masruq bin Al-Ajda’, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Ansari and Shurayh. So I asked them and they said: We do not like to take the Book of God as a price."
"20578","(20578) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah, that he disliked selling the Qur’an. And he bought it."
"20579","(20579) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Muhammad, on the authority of Sa`id Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: I wish I had seen hands being cut off while selling the Qur’an."
"20580","(20580) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The anus is more beloved to me. Whoever sells the Qur’an, but he hates taking a fee for displaying it."
"20581","(20581) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated selling the Qur’an, and he said: It is for whoever reads from Ahl al-Bayt, and he hates the book, there is a reward for it."
"20582","(20582) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Salem, who said: An evil business is the sale of the Qur’an."
"20583","(20583) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah, He hated buying and selling the Qur’an."
"20584","(20584) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I wished that I saw hands being cut off while selling the Qur’an."
"20585","(20585) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: Alqamiya used to hate selling the Qur’an."
"20586","(20586) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, that Ibn Sirin hated buying and selling them."
"20587","(20587) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, he said: I asked Shurayh and Masruq, And Abdullah bin Yazid, about selling the Qur’an, they said: Do not take the Book of God as a price."
"20588","(20588) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I said to Al-‘Alqamah: Should I sell a Qur’an? He said: No."
"20589","(20589) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that he said: He bought it, And do not sell it."
"20590","(20590) Ismail bin Ibrahim and Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas that he permitted Concerning the purchase of the Qur’an and the reluctance to sell it."
"20591","(20591) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, the same."
"20592","(20592) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He bought it, And do not sell it."
"20593","(20593) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: There is no harm in buying it."
"20594","(20594) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, that he saw no harm in buying the Qur’an, and that He will be given a reward for writing it."
"20595","(20595) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of his leaders, who said: Buy, and do not sell."
"20596","(20596) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Uzza, who said: Al-Sha’bi ordered me to sell."
"20597","(20597) Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: I asked Abu Salama, about He sold the Qur’an, and said: Buy it, but do not sell it."
"20598","(20598) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah and Al-Shu’biy, that they used to make concessions in Selling the Qur’an."
"20599","(20599) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, that he said: They do not sell books. By God, they only sell paper and the work of their own hands."
"20600","(20600) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he had no intention of buying or selling them. It's unfortunate"
"20601","(20601) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Matar al-Warraq, on the authority of al-Hasan and al-Sha’abi that they were not He sees harm in selling the Qur’an."
"20602","(20602) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Hasan that he did not see any harm in buying or selling them."
"20603","(20603) Qasim bin Malik Al-Muzani narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Aidh, who said: I said to Al-Sha’bi: Here are our people. They write the Qur’an for a reward. He said: As for you, do not do it."
"20604","(20604) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, that he was forced to co-write it."
"20605","(20605) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of his brother Isa, on the authority of his father Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Layla said that a Christian from the people of Al-Hira wrote him a Qur’an for ninety dirhams."
"20606","(20606) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated writing the Qur’an for the reward and interpreted This verse {So woe to those who write the Book with their own hands}"
"20607","(20607) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya that he wanted to write He wrote a Qur’an, so he sought help from his companions and wrote it down."
"20608","(20608) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father, that he did not see any harm in giving him something based on his book. It means reward."
"20609","(20609) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he used to hate it. To give her a reward for her writing."
"20610","(20610) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I was with Ibn Omar walking in the market, when we were with people from The slavers had gathered to seize a slave girl. When they saw Ibn Umar, they moved away and said: Ibn Umar has come, and Ibn Umar approached her. Omar touched part of her body and said: Where are the companions of this slave girl? She is only a commodity."
"20611","(20611) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that if he wanted to He buys the slave girl and places his hand on her buttocks, or between her thighs, and perhaps revealing her legs."
"20612","(20612) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ubaid al-Muttab, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of a man from Abdullah’s companions, He said: I don't care whether you touch it, or whether you touch this wall."
"20613","(20613) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Habib, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, that he bargained with his maidservant and put his hand on her. Her breasts and chest."
"20614","(20614) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: I heard Ata’ being asked about the slave girls who were followed in Mecca. He hated looking at them except for someone who wanted to buy them."
"20615","(20615) Azhar al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: When Muhammad was sent to him with a slave girl, he would look at her. He revealed between her legs and arms."
"20616","(20616) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that a black friend of his wrote to him to buy He has a maidservant, so he did so, and he touched part of the maidservant’s leg. He said: That reached the blackness of his speech, and he said: I do not like it. She looked at her legs, but I am not like this and that."
"20617","(20617) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Hakim al-Athram, on the authority of Abu Tamimah, on the authority of Abu Musa that He addressed them and said: I do not know of a man who bought a female slave and looked at what is below the body and what is above the knees without that I will punish him."
"20618","(20618) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he disliked buying something for the purpose of giving. And the harvest, but it is called the month."
"20619","(20619) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’, or Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Do not surrender to Juice, nor to the tender, nor to the threshing floor, meaning the threshing floor."
"20620","(20620) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, something like this."
"20621","(20621) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, he said: Do not sell to the harvest, nor to Grandparents, nor to study, but name a month."
"20622","(20622) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Muhammad was asked about selling to a giver, and he said: I do not know what."
"20623","(20623) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’: He hated it."
"20624","(20624) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, that he disliked selling to Giving"
"20625","(20625) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Dhabi bin Amr narrated to us, saying: I asked Salim, about the advance until one attains the fruit, and he said: No, except to A fixed term."
"20626","(20626) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair bin Atiq, who said: I said to Saeed bin Jubayr, “Buy until the harvest.” And to the lesson? He said: Buy a specified amount for a specified period."
"20627","(20627) Hafs bin Ghayath and Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Habib, that the mothers of the believers were They buy to give."
"20628","(20628) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, that Ibn Umar used to buy for a gift."
"20629","(20629) Hafs bin Ghayath and Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ja’far bin Amr bin Harith, on the authority of his father that He sent Ali a brocade dress woven with gold, and Hafs said: It was drawn with gold, so Amr bin Harith bought it from him. For four thousand dirhams as a gift."
"20630","(20630) Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, on the authority of Nuh bin Abi Bilal, who said: Ali bin Hussein bought from me for his giving. food"
"20631","(20631) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no harm in selling to a giver."
"20632","(20632) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Hakim bin Raziq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab in Al-Birr. With flour, he said: It is usury."
"20633","(20633) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He used to hate the market with wheat and its food."
"20634","(20634) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm in wheat with flour, and wheat with stalks. Flour for wheat, bread for wheat, and a penny for a penny, hand in hand."
"20635","(20635) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad was asked about bread made from wheat. He said: Bread from wheat."
"20636","(20636) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about wheat with flour. His thoughts"
"20637","(20637) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: He used to crush wheat in the stalk."
"20638","(20638) Ubaidah bin Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amer, who said: He was asked about someone who drives wheat. He said: He said: If He is not a unique lord."
"20639","(20639) Wakī’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bā, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammād about qafiz of wheat with qafiz of fine flour. His thoughts"
"20640","(20640) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he disliked it except one weight for another."
"20641","(20641) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he disliked it except one weight for another weight."
"20642","(20642) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, that he disliked it except one weight for another weight."
"20643","(20643) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, who said: I heard Al-Sha’bi say: Salvation is not for anything, whoever sells It was sold and it was due to its owner, and the seller is responsible for the price for which he took it. He does not owe anything more than that."
"20644","(20444) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: No one is required to be saved except a fool. As you sold, or return it as you received."
"20645","(20645) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, that he did not see salvation as anything."
"20646","(20646) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Othman Al-Batti, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Ali was good at salvation."
"20647","(20447) Yahya bin Ali Al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, that a man left His wife, his son, and his maidservant, so he sold his wife and his son to the maidservant, and he who had bought her had sexual intercourse with her, and she gave birth. Then the owner of the slave girl came and became attached to her, so he disputed with Ali and said: Ali: You sold your wife and your son, and she was born to a man. He handed over the transaction, and the man said: I adjure you by God when you decide according to the Book of God. So he said: Take your maidservant and her two children, and he said to the other: Take The woman and the son agreed to be saved, so when the other took the sale, he handed over the sale."
"20648","(20648) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Salamah Ibn Alqamiya, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: The ruling was It rules that whoever sells something that does not belong to him, then it belongs to its owner if he asks for it, and this is taken for granted."
"20649","(20649) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, that a woman sold a house to her husband while he was absent, so when he came He refused to approve the sale, so he disputed it to Iyas bin Muawiyah, so he made the buyer say: May God bless you. She spent two thousand dirhams on it, and he said: The loss is upon me, the loss is upon me. He said: So he judged the man in his house and ordered his wife to the prison. When he saw that, he permitted the sale."
"20650","(20650) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, that he saw salvation as a strong condition and he stressed Therein"
"20651","(20651) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not see salvation as anything."
"20652","(20652) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Fulfil, who said: I asked Anas about the witnesses for slaves, and he said: permissible"
"20653","(20653) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amir, that Shurayh permitted the witness of the slave."
"20654","(20654) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to reward her for minor matters."
"20655","(20655) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ammar al-Dhani, who said: I witnessed Sharih who had a slave over his house. So he confirmed his testimony, and he was told: He is a slave, so he said: We are all slaves and our mother is Eve."
"20656","(20656) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: Shurayh said: We do not allow the witnesses of slaves, so he said Ali: No, we used to do it. He said: Then Shurayh was still doing it except for his mistress."
"20657","(20657) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It is not permissible for a slave to witness."
"20658","(20658) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is not permissible for a slave to witness."
"20659","(20659) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Rashid, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: It is not permissible for a slave to witness."
"20660","(20660) Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata, who said: It is not permissible The witness of the servant, even if it is in a minor matter."
"20661","(20661) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, regarding his saying: {And seek martyrdom. Two witnesses from your men. He said: from the free."
"20662","(20662) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amir, who said: It is not permissible for a slave to bear witness."
"20663","(20663) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Ezza, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi that he rejected the testimony of Abd."
"20664","(20664) I heard Waki` saying: Sufyan said: It is not permissible for a slave to witness. Abu Bakr said: This is the opinion of Waki`."
"20665","(20645) Waki’ told us, he said: Hassan bin Saleh told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: The people of Mecca do not They reward us with a dirham."
"20666","(20646) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If the mortgager and the mortgagee disagreed, and he said: This: Ten, and this man said: twenty, so the saying is the saying of the bettor."
"20667","(20667) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: The statement is the statement of the one who is mortgaged."
"20668","(20668) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The statement is the statement of the one in whose hand is the mortgage."
"20669","(20669) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Iyas ibn Muawiyah, who said: If the mortgager and the mortgager disagree The statement is the statement of the mortgager unless evidence is established, and everyone who has something in his possession. A saying is a saying."
"20670","(20670) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awan, on the authority of Qatada, who said: If the bettor and the mortgager disagree, then the statement is the opinion of the mortgager. What is between it and its value, so if it increases, then the statement is the statement of the bettor."
"20671","(20671) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the bettor disagrees As for the mortgager, the statement is the statement of the mortgagee, unless the mortgagee evaluates the evidence."
"20672","(20672) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Hisham, on the authority of Amer, who said: If the mortgager and the mortgagee disagree about the value of The mortgage is clear to the one who claims the mortgage."
"20673","(20673) Ar’ara bin Al-Barand narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik al-Azraq, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, He said: The statement is the statement of the mortgagee."
"20674","(20674) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, who said: Hammad was asked about a man who has a mortgage in his hand. He said: It is ten, and his companion said: It is a dirham, and he said: The clear statement is on the one who claims credit, as if he had said: It is a mortgage, and its owner said: It is a deposit. This was the statement of the owner of the property."
"20675","(20675) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The statement is the statement of the mortgager."
"20676","(20676) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Jafar, that when the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came out, he would command Ali to He cuts the walls."
"20677","(20677) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn Abi Hakam Al-Ghaffari saying: My grandmother narrated to me, on the authority of a paternal uncle. Abi Rafi’ bin Amr Al-Ghafari said: I, as a boy, was throwing palm trees for the Ansar, and it was said to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: There is a boy here who throws our palm trees. He was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Boy, why do you throw? Palm trees? I said: Eat. He said: Do not throw away the palm trees and eat whatever falls below them. Then he wiped his head and said: Oh God, satisfy his stomach.\n(Tirmidhi 1288 and Abu Dawud 2615)"
"20678","(20678) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, He said: I heard a man from Muzina asking the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the fruits that were in their sleeves. He said: Who? If he ate with his mouth and did not take it out, there is no blame on him. (Tirmidhi 1289, Ahmed 207)"
"20679","(20679) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of Harun bin Ri’ab, on the authority of Sinan bin Salamah, he said: He narrated to us while he was in Bahrain. He said: I was with a group of young men picking dates, then Omar came to us, and the boys ran, so I got up and said: O Commander of the Faithful, this is among the It caused a fart, and he said: Show me it. When I showed it, he said: Go. I said: O Commander of the Faithful, you will see these wandering young men. If you depart from me, they will take away what is with me. He said: So he walked with me until I reached my safety."
"20680","(20680) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, he said: I asked Hammad about that which falls from the palm trees. Not for you? He said: Ibrahim said: The early immigrants did not see any harm in eating food."
"20681","(20681) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Ayyad, who said: Omar said: If you pass In a garden, eat, and do not take food for yourself."
"20682","(20682) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: We used to fight and get a share of the fruits, but we did not see that. It's unfortunate"
"20683","(20683) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, he said: I asked Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, I said: I may have gone out to Idiot, so we pass by palm trees and eat from them and from trees, and both of them made concessions to me and said: Unless they bear fruit or spoil it."
"20684","(20684) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: If you pass by an orchard, call His companion, if he responds to you, then ask him for food, and if he does not respond to you, then eat, and do not do evil."
"20685","(20685) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Zainab, who said: I traveled in an army with Abu Bakra. And Abu Barzah and Abd al-Rahman bin Samarra, and we used to eat from the fruits."
"20686","(20686) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I was traveling with him, and he He eats from the fruits."
"20687","(20687) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Whoever passes by a wall, let him eat, but not carry. (Ahmed 224)"
"20688","(20688) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: There is no harm in the fruits of non-Muslims."
"20689","(20689) Wakī’ narrated to us, he said: Yazid bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I asked Ubaydah, about Ibn The path passes by the fruit and says: It may be eaten and not spoiled."
"20690","(20690) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I asked Ubaydah and he mentioned something similar."
"20691","(20691) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Shu`abi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juniy, who said: I heard Jundub al-Bajlili saying: We used to go on a campaign with the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we would do as they do, so we would take some of the fruit and take He guides us from one village to another without us participating in their homes."
"20692","(20692) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Hammad about a traveler who eats from the fruit, and he said: When they wrong them. The princes I prefer not to eat, and I asked the arbiter and he said: Eat."
"20693","(20693) Shababi told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abbad bin Shurahbil, a man from Banu Ghubr. He said: We were struck by a tooth, so I entered a wall and took a tooth and rubbed it, then the owner of the wall came and hit me and took my clothes. Then we came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: You did not feed him when he was hungry or hungry, nor did you teach him when he was ignorant. And he took his dress and spread it over his friend. (Abu Dawud 2413 and Ibn Majah 2298)"
"20694","(20694) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman A servant of Saad, he said: We went down to the wall of two palaces, and he said to Saad: If it pleases you to be a true Muslim, then do not let him harm you. Something, and he gave me a dirham, and said: Buy some of it fruit, or food and part of it fodder."
"20695","(20695) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: So You pass by a palm tree, or something similar, and a wall has been surrounded by it, so do not enter it except with the permission of its owner, and if you pass by it in a clearing, The land, eat it, but do not bear it."
"20696","(20696) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, he said: Yazeed ibn al-Asam narrated to us, he said: I met Aisha. It was coming from Mecca, with I and Ibn Talha ibn Ubad Allah, who is her sister’s son, and we had fallen into one of the walls. Medina, so we ate from it, and that reached her, so she came to her sister’s son, blaming him and berating him, then she came to me. So you gave me an eloquent admonition."
"20697","(20697) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Do not eat of the fruit except for the price."
"20698","(20698) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abd al-A’la al-Ja’fi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr said: Do not eat of the fruit except with the permission of its family."
"20699","(20699) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said : He would not protect the fruit if it had no wall, nor would he eat from the wall except with the permission of its family."
"20700","(20700) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Fudail bin Ghazwan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Hazim, he said: I asked Mujahid about He fell from the tree and said: Leave it to the wild beasts and the birds."
"20701","(20701) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Nafi`, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he disliked catching people."
"20702","(20702) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Yahya, on the authority of his father, that Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein were They accept the rewards of Muawiyah."
"20703","(20703) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Habib, who said: I saw Ibn Omar and Ibn Abbas bring you gifts. The chosen one accepts it."
"20704","(20704) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Simak ibn Salamah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ismah, he said: I was with Aisha was brought to her by a messenger from Mu'awiyah, and she accepted it."
"20705","(20705) Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, that Aisha was sent to her Mu'awiya's necklace was valued at one hundred thousand, so she accepted it and divided it among the mothers of the believers."
"20706","(20706) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, who said: Send Bishr bin Marwan with me. With five hundred to five people: to Abu Juhayfa, to Abu Razin, to Amr bin Maymun, to Muriya, and to Abu Abd. Al-Rahman, Abu Razin, Abu Juhayfa and Amr ibn Maymun rejected it, and the other two accepted it."
"20707","(20707) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Umayr, who mentioned a hadith similar to Yahya bin Saeed."
"20708","(20708) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, who said: I heard Al-Hasan and a man asked him, and he said: The worker came So he will give me and reward me? He said: Take her, you have no father and go."
"20709","(20709) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Qais, who said: I entered with my father to Abu Bakr, so that we would visit him. He was sick, so we mounted him on two horses, and I saw the names tattooed on his hands, flying from him."
"20710","(20710) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour and Ibrahim bin Muhajir, that Ibrahim and Tamim bin They greeted him, they went out to a worker, and he preferred Tamim to Abraham for the reward, so Abraham became angry."
"20711","(20711) Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, that Khalid ibn Asid sent thirty thousand to Masruq, and he returned them and said to him: If you had taken them, given them in charity and brought them with them, he refused. He took it."
"20712","(20712) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah, that he did not see With generous workers’ rewards."
"20713","(20713) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he rode to a worker and he granted him permission and carried him on an animal. So he accepted it."
"20714","(20714) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: There is no harm in workers’ rewards."
"20715","(20715) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: There is no harm in workers’ rewards."
"20716","(20716) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hamid, that Ibn Hubira approved of Al-Hasan And early, they accepted, and he granted Muhammad permission, but he did not accept from him."
"20717","(20717) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, that a man was sent to Dhar with his reward, and he said to the Messenger: Eat a Muslim. Was he sent with this? He said: No, he said: He rejected it, and he said: {No, it is a matter of contention for grilling}"
"20718","(20718) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn Mina, That Abdulaziz bin Marwan was sent to Ibn Omar, who accepted, and he was sent to Abdullah bin Ayash Ibn Abi Rabi’ah, and he did not It will be accepted from him."
"20719","(20719) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Ali said: There is no harm in the workers’ reward. Indeed, He has help and provision, and He only gave you from the goodness of His wealth."
"20720","(20720) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If I had come to a worker and he had rewarded me, I would have accepted from him. Rather, it is in the same position as the treasury. The bad and the good can enter it, and he said: If the mail comes to you regarding a matter of disobedience, then do not He is good about his reward, and if he brings you something in which there is no problem, then there is no problem with his reward."
"20721","(20721) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of a man he did not name, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Amer. Bin Hudhaim, that Omar rewarded him with a thousand dinars."
"20722","(20722) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, he said: Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’tha’i narrated to me, he said: We set out as thirty riders. We have the lions. Bishr bin Marwan ordered him and rewarded him with fifty dinars, so he accepted it."
"20723","(20723) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Mu’ammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that he did not see anything wrong with a man selling his brother from Breastfeeding"
"20724","(20724) Mu’ammar narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin and his followers, who said: There is no harm for a man to sell His breastfeeding brother"
"20725","(20725) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: There is no harm in it."
"20726","(20726) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mansur, that he used to say: A man sells his breastfed brother. And his mother, there is no problem with that."
"20727","(20727) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I wrote to Nafi’ asking him about the sale of a breastfed brother, and he said: It's okay"
"20728","(20728) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi and Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid said that he hated for a man to sell his foster brother."
"20729","(20729) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said about his sister and his breastfeeding grandmother, he thought about He sold them."
"20730","(20730) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Imran al-Qattan, who said: I heard al-Hasan and he was asked about his thoughts. So I mentioned it to his commander, and he said: Jabir bin Zaid used to say it, and Ibrahim Al-Nakha’i used to say: He could sell it if he wanted."
"20731","(20731) Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he disliked selling his foster brother."
"20732","(20732) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: A man came to Abdullah He said: My maid breastfed my son. Shall I not sell her? He said: Then Abdullah said: I wish he had taken her out to the market and said: Who will buy the mother of my children from me? It is as if he hated her."
"20733","(20733) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymiy, who said: I asked Al-Hasan about the Almighty’s saying: {And give witness when You have pledged allegiance. He said: Don’t you see that his saying: {And if some of you believe in one another} means that he thought that he had abrogated what was Before him"
"20734","(20734) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: I said to Al-Sha’bi: Have you seen a man buying something from another man? He must bear witness, is it necessary? He said: No, don't you see what he said: {And if some of you believe in others}"
"20735","(20735) Muhammad bin Marwan told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Nadhrah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri in his saying: {And bear witness when you pledge allegiance} He said: I abrogated it {And if some of you believe in one another}"
"20736","(20736) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Razi, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, who said: I saw Safwan ibn Mahrez and he came. He went to the market with fake dirhams and said: Who will sell me good grapes for an evil dirham? He bought them and did not bear witness."
"20737","(20737) Ibn Abi Za’idah told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, who said: I heard the ruling recited: (Then if some of you believe in others) He said: These witnesses have been abrogated."
"20738","(20738) Ibn Abi Za’idah told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There are three types of sales: the sale of witnesses and a book. He sold with accepted proof, and he sold with trust, then he recited the verse about religion."
"20739","(20739) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Moses said: There are three whose supplications will not be answered: a man who gives his wealth to a fool, and God says: {And do not give your wealth to fools.} And a man had a wife of bad character, but he did not separate from her or divorce her, and a man bought a marriage but did not testify."
"20740","(20740) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Three are not answered. They have a claim: a man who supplicates against his wife and his slaves, and a man who buys and sells, but does not bear witness."
"20741","(20741) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he used to say: He bears witness when he sells and when He bought it."
"20742","(20742) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, that he used to say: He bears witness when he sells and when he buys."
"20743","(20743) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of a man from the family of Abi Al-Hijaj, on the authority of Abi Al-Hijaj, he said: Ali used me Ali Al-Sawad and commanded me to make the People of the Book swear by God."
"20744","(20744) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Marwan ibn Muawiyah, on the authority of Yahya ibn Misra, on the authority of Amr ibn Murr, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah said that he made the polytheist swear by God."
"20745","(20745) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Masruq, that he used to swear Those who associate God with Allah."
"20746","(20746) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The polytheist should not swear except by God. But he is harsh on him regarding his religion."
"20747","(20747) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that Ka’b ibn Sur took him into the church. And he placed the Torah on his head and asked him to swear to God."
"20748","(20748) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh, that it was The polytheists will swear to God where they hate Him."
"20749","(20749) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ghusn, he said: I heard Al-Sha’bi and he wanted to swear an oath as a Christian, so he said: Do I swear to God? Al-Sha’bi said: You have forsaken God while you are seeing. Take him to the market and swear to him according to what he swears by. People of their religion"
"20750","(20750) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid, on the authority of Ata, who said: He was asked about the Jew and the Christian. Should he swear by the Torah and the Gospel? He said: Make him swear by God, for the Torah and the Gospel are from the Book of God."
"20751","(20751) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Shurayh, that he used to swear by the polytheists. With their religion"
"20752","(20752) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Dinar, who said: I asked Salim and Tawoos about selling the skins of dead people. He thought about it, and Salem said: Is the skin of a dead person sold except as eating its flesh?"
"20753","(20753) Yahya bin Sa’id al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Salama Abi Bishr, on the authority of Ikrimah, that he disliked selling skins The dead and the sacrifice."
"20754","(20754) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu al-Walid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who raised it, saying: When God forbids A people who ate something whose price was forbidden to them. (Abu Dawud 3482, Ibn Hibban 4938)"
"20755","(20755) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, he said: Mughiryah, the client of Amr bin Harith, told me: Al-Sha’bi was asked about The skins of dead buffaloes that he sold before they were tanned."
"20756","(20756) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They were reluctant to sell her. So they eat its price, meaning the skins of the dead."
"20757","(20757) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he was reluctant to sell it and wear it before he Get tanned"
"20758","(20758) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he disliked selling the skins of the dead until they were tanned."
"20759","(20759) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jafar, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace in the year of the conquest, saying: God and His Messenger have forbidden the selling of the dead.\n(Bukhari 2236, Muslim 1207)"
"20760","(20760) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, he said: Al-Qasim narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Imamah, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade one to hoard food. (Hakim 11/2. Tabarani 7776)"
"20761","(20761) Yahya bin Sa’id al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Mawla. Al-Ansar, on the authority of Uthman ibn Affan, who forbade hukrah."
"20762","(20762) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, On the authority of Muammar Ibn Nadlah al-Adawi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No one monopolizes except a sinner.\n(Muslim 1227. Abu Dawud 3440)"
"20763","(20763) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibn Omar, He said: Hiccup is a sin."
"20764","(20764) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, who said: Omar said: Whoever monopolizes food, then gives it in charity. With his capital and the profit he was not atone for it."
"20765","(20765) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Ali was informed of a man who hoarded food worth a hundred thousand, so he ordered him to It gets burned."
"20766","(20766) Humaid bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Rawasi told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Qays, who said: Hubaysh said: Ali burned his black yader. I would have monopolized it. If he had left it, I would have won it like the kufa’s `Ata’."
"20767","(20767) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Babah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: Only a sinner or a transgressor monopolizes it."
"20768","(20768) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Habib, on the authority of Nawfal ibn Abdul-Malik, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the rule of the country. (Harith 427)"
"20769","(20769) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Asbagh bin Zaid Al-Warraq told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Abi Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Kathir ibn Muriya al-Hadrami, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Whoever monopolizes food for forty nights, he has disavowed himself from God and Allah has disavowed him, and as long as the people of Arṣḥ remained among them, a hungry man remained. I am absolved from them under the protection of God.\n(Ahmad 33. Abu Ali 5720)"
"20770","Abu Abdul Rahman Baqi Ibn Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Shayba told us, he said:\n(20770) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he did not see It is unfortunate that a man gives another man a garment and says: Sell it for such-and-such, and whatever you add is yours."
"20771","(20771) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin that he did not see any harm."
"20772","(20772) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Mutarrif, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Shurayh that he did not see It is unfortunate that he gives him the garment and says: Sell this garment for such-and-such, and as much as you have, you have it."
"20773","(20773) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir that he did not see any harm in that."
"20774","(20774) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: If a man gives an item to another man and he says: What you prefer, It is yours, or between you and me, there is no problem with it."
"20775","(20775) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Saleh, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Concerning a man giving another man a garment and saying: Sell it for such-and-such, so whatever is more between you and me, he says: There is no problem with it."
"20776","(20776) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, and on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that they hated it."
"20777","(20777) Hakam Al-Razi told us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Ata’, that he did not see any harm in that. He said: He was a peacock. He hates it except for a known reward."
"20778","(20778) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man giving another man a garment and saying: Sell it for such-and-such, and whatever you spare, it is yours. He said: If it is for cash, there is no problem. And if it is by his wife, then there is no good in her."
"20779","(20779) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Masoud: He saw no harm in a man selling twelve possessions unless he took To spend profit."
"20780","(20780) Abd bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, that he disliked it if he sold A man who makes a profit is that he takes profit for his expenses."
"20781","(20781) Abd al-Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan, that he did not think of that. It's unfortunate"
"20782","(20782) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, that he saw no harm in taking money for spending. Profit"
"20783","(20783) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: There is no harm in calculating the maintenance on Heirlooms"
"20784","(20784) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ajlan, who said: I said to Ibrahim: We will buy goods, then We will increase the value of the property and the rent, then we will sell it to him for a profit. He said: There is no problem with it."
"20785","(20785) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Tawus, that he was asked about a man who buys fine linen and hides it for him, Shall I take his profit? He said: If he makes it clear."
"20786","(20786) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; What about a man who sells his property at a profit and takes the profit for rent? He said: He takes the profit from what was sold in the land from which he came out, if he wishes, and from what was sold in the country in which he sold it, he does not take its profit."
"20787","(20787) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: That is falsehood."
"20788","(20788) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amir, who said: Do not take your goods and take with them some leftovers."
"20789","(20789) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, he said: I asked Ibrahim, about a man who sold tea from a man, then he exchanged it for him. Before he took it, he said: Give me a ride, but he refused, and said: Give me a dirham and I will tell you what he thought."
"20790","(20790) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Alqama A man sold an animal, and its owner wanted to return it and return the dirhams with it, so Alqamah said: This is our animal, so what do we have to do with it? Your money?"
"20791","(20791) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, that he hated to return it. And he will return a dirham with it."
"20792","(20792) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’bad, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Zayd being asked about a man who bought a house or real estate, and he wanted to If he told him, but he refused, so he left him ten dirhams, or twenty dirhams, and he told him, he said: There is no problem with that."
"20793","(20793) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that he hated to return it and he would return it. She has a dirham."
"20794","(20794) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Asama bin Zayd, who said: I heard Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab being asked about a man who bought a camel. Then the buyer regretted it and wanted to return it and return with him eight dirhams, so Sa`id said: There is no harm in it, but the usury is What is eaten and drunk is measured and weighed."
"20795","(20795) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Two men came and stood at Shurayh, then They had a conversation, and one of them said to him: Bear witness that I have accepted a camel and thirty dirhams, but Shurayh remained silent, and he said: So I see him. He hated it because he denied it."
"20796","(20796) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin that they did not see that. It is unfortunate if a man takes advantage of the sale."
"20797","(20797) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdullah bin Abi Mughith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, about a man who bought a camel and wanted to return it and return the dirhams that he had with him, so he said: There is no problem with it."
"20798","(20798) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; Concerning a man who buys a commodity and then exploits it. He said: There is no harm in him returning it and returning his dirhams with it."
"20799","(20799) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If it changes from its current state, there is no problem."
"20800","(20800) Ali bin Musahir and Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Sadiqa bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of his grandfather Rihah bin Al-Harith, On the authority of Ammar bin Yasser, he said: A slave is better than two slaves, a camel is better than two camels, and a garment is better than two camels. Two garments, there is no problem with it hand in hand. Usury is only for women, except for what is measured and weighed."
"20801","(20801) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar that he bought a camel for four camels. With Al-Rabadhi, and he said to his owner: Go and see, and if you are satisfied, then the sale is obligatory."
"20802","(20802) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin al-Hanafi, who said: I told him: Should I sell a camel for two camels for a certain period? He said: No, and there is no harm in it, hand in hand."
"20803","(20803) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The animal is one with two and is not fit, meaning female. (Tirmidhi 1338 and Ibn Majah 2271)"
"20804","(20804) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hikam. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade, on the authority of The animal is one with two, meaning a female."
"20805","(20805) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, who said: He sold Ali had one camel for two camels, and the one from whom he had bought it said to him: Hand over my camel to me until I bring you your camel, so he said Ali: My hand will not depart from its muzzle until it brings my camel."
"20806","(20806) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir that He saw no harm in the camel or the two camels."
"20807","(20807) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said: There is no problem. By the camel, by the camel."
"20808","(20808) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim and al-Shu`biyy, he said: I said to them: What do you see? In a tongue with two tongues, and in a source of water with two sources? Al-Sha’bi said: There is no harm in it, and Ibrahim hated it."
"20809","(20809) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail ibn Umayyah, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: No. It is good in the Coptic language."
"20810","(20810) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Ali, who said: There is no harm in being permissible. With the two solutions."
"20811","(20811) Ali bin Mushir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Everything that cannot be measured or weighed, there is no problem in He gives one for two, or three, or less, or more, hand in hand."
"20812","(20812) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The animal is one for another, there is no harm in it hand to hand, and there is no good in it with regard to women."
"20813","(20813) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Anas Ibn Sirin, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: The camel. With camels? He said: Hand in hand? I said: No, he said: He thought of it."
"20814","(20814) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no harm in a camel for two camels. Women"
"20815","(20815) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of al-Sanabih al-Ahmasi, he said: The Prophet received his sight. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, a beautiful she-camel, and he said: What is this she-camel? He said: O Messenger of God, I brought her back with two camels. He said: So yes, then."
"20816","(20816) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, he said: The Messenger of God forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of animal for animal, we forget. (Ahmad 12. Dharmi 2564)"
"20817","(20817) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Abu Al-Hasan Al-Barrad, on the authority of Ali, said: An animal is not treated with other animals, nor is a sheep treated with two sheep, except hand to hand."
"20818","(20818) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Omar was asked about the tea. With two sheep to the living, meaning fertile, so he thought of that."
"20819","(20819) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafla, who said: There is no problem. On horseback, on two horses and on mount, on two mounts, hand in hand."
"20820","(20820) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: I asked Ayyub about wearing two garments forgot, he said: It was Muhammad. He hates it"
"20821","(20821) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He bought Safiyya for seven heads. (Muslim 1045. Abu Dawud 2990)"
"20822","(20822) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Wazi`, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: Who will sell to me? One camel for two camels, who will sell me a camel for two she-camels?"
"20823","(20823) Abbad told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: There is no harm in white, with two eggs and two walnuts. With two nuts."
"20824","(2[corrupt]824) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah Mawla Mujahid, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: There is no problem. With the white, with the two eggs, and the walnut, with the two nuts, hand in hand."
"20825","(20825) Mulazim bin Amr told us, on the authority of Zufar bin Zayd, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked Abu Hurairah about purchasing He kept the two sheep for a certain period of time, but he forbade me and said: No, except hand to hand."
"20826","(20826) Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no harm in saying to the slave: “He will do so and so in cash, and he will do so and so on his offspring,” but they should not separate except with their consent."
"20827","(20827) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, or on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: Two transactions in one transaction is usury, unless the man says: If it is for cash, then for such and such, and if it is for his share. So this is how"
"20828","(20828) Waki’, said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd Allah, on the authority of his father, with a similar story."
"20829","(20829) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, that he hated for a man to touch a commodity, saying: He criticized such-and-such, and he criticized such-and-such."
"20830","(20830) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab that he heard him forbidding The two transactions include the deal."
"20831","(20831) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus that he heard it, he said: There is no harm in it if he takes it against someone. The two types."
"20832","(20832) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ataa, they said: There is no harm in him saying: This garment is for this money, and this garment is for this, and he goes with it on One of them"
"20833","(20833) Yahya bin Abi Zaidah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who bought something, then said: I don’t have this, I will buy it for the women. He said: If they leave the sale, then buy it. I wish"
"20834","(20834) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever sells two sales in a sale is entitled to the equivalent of both, or usury. (Tirmidhi 1231, Abu Dawud 3455)"
"20835","(20835) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, that when his grandfather sent out merchants, he would There are two conditions in the sale."
"20836","(20836) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, he said: I asked the arbitrator, and Hammad, about a man who buys from another man. He says: If it is for money, then for such and such, and if it is for a time, then for such and such. He said: There is no problem if he deviates from one of the two. He said: Shu`ba, so I mentioned that to Mughiriya, and he said: Abraham did not see any harm in that if he separated over one of them."
"20837","(20837) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade May the peace and blessings of God be upon him from selling loyalty, and from gifting it. (Bukhari 2535. Muslim 1145)"
"20838","(20838) Jarir, Hafs, and Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: Loyalty cannot be sold or given."
"20839","(20839) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: Loyalty is only like lineage. Should a man sell? His lineage"
"20840","(20840) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Ali said: Loyalty is in his position. The oath, it is not to be sold or given away. Confirm it where God has placed it."
"20841","(20841) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Omar, who said: Loyalty is like kinship. It will be sold or given away."
"20842","(20842) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Loyalty is like lineage, it cannot be sold, nor can it be sold. Yahweh"
"20843","(20843) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Miskin, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Loyalty cannot be sold, nor Yahweh"
"20844","(20844) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: Loyalty is not sold, nor is it given, nor He gives it in charity."
"20845","(20845) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: Loyalty is flesh like the flesh of lineage, not It will be sold or given away."
"20846","(20846) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: It was not He sees harm in selling loyalty if it is from his office, and he hates it if it is freeing."
"20847","(20847) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Loyalty cannot be sold or given."
"20848","(20848) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafli, who said: Loyalty is like lineage, it cannot be sold, nor Yahweh"
"20849","(20849) Sufyan bin Uyayn narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, who said: Maymunah pledged allegiance to Sulayman bin Yasar to Ibn Abbas"
"20850","(20850) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I asked Abraham about a man who freed another man, and the freed man went off and befriended someone else. He said: He has no right to do that unless the freedman gifts it to him."
"20851","(20851) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm, that A woman from the presence of a warrior who pledged her slave’s loyalty to herself and freed him, so he freed himself. He said: So he gave himself to a slave. Al-Rahman bin Amr bin Hazm, he said: She died while the loyalist disputed with Uthman bin Affan, so Uthman called with clear evidence for what he said: So he brought him clear evidence, and Uthman said to him: Go and befriend whomever you wish. So Abd al-Rahman bin Amr bin Hazm appointed him as governor."
"20852","(20852) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Ibrahim and Al-Shu’bi, who said: There is no harm in selling loyalty. Al-Sa'ib and his wife"
"20853","(20853) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, that a woman who pledged loyalty She is loyal to her husband, and Hisham bin Hubira said: As for me, I see him as a servant to her husband as long as he lives, so if he dies, I will return him to her. The woman inherited"
"20854","(20854) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The predecessors disliked something that they did not have. People's hands are the origin.q"
"20855","(20855) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: When Ibn Umar was asked about the man He buys something from a man for a specified period of time, but he does not have the basis for it, and he does not see any harm in it. Yahya said: Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab is hated."
"20856","(20856) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, that he used to hate the predecessors except in something that he had control over. Its origin. Ayoub said: I was informed of a peacock like that."
"20857","(20857) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he saw no harm in paying advances until a specified period. Its origin is with him, or it was not. He said: And Muhammad disliked the predecessors except in one matter with his companion."
"20858","(20858) Yahya bin Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He does not say hello in anything except from it. Something in people's hands."
"20859","(20859) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim: that Ali and Shuraih used to guarantee the worker."
"20860","(20860) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ibn Ubaid bin Al-Abraz, that Ali guaranteed a carpenter."
"20861","(20861) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Husayn Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, He said: Whoever takes a reward is guarantor."
"20862","(20862) Abbad told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, the same."
"20863","(20863) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Khaled Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utba bin Masoud, who said: The hired worker. He is guaranteed his reward, a guarantee for what was entrusted to him."
"20864","(20864) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the joint employee takes something, he is liable."
"20865","(20865) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: Whenever he bought He hired someone to carry it for the thing. The ruling said: He guarantees it."
"20866","(20866) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid is similar to a comprehensive hadith."
"20867","(20867) Azhar al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, that he did not guarantee the wage-earner except through neglect."
"20868","(20868) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Every worker who takes a wage is liable, except for the one who An arrogant enemy, or one who is more helpful than yours."
"20869","(20869) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no guarantee on the employee who works for consultations."
"20870","(20870) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, that he did not guarantee the sailor’s drowning, nor Burning"
"20871","(20871) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hasan narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Salih bin Dinar, that Ali, may God be pleased with him, used to guarantee Joint employee."
"20872","(20872) Waki’ narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham Al-Attar, who said: I hired a porter to carry something for me. So he broke it, so I disputed with him to Sharih, and he took it for granted, and said: He only hired you to convey it to him, and he did not hire you to break it."
"20873","(20873) Abu Bakr narrated to us, Hasan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhayr Al-Ansi, that a man hired a man to work on He struck a camel and gouged out its eye, so he disputed with it to a segment and secured it, and said: He only hired you to make amends and did not hire you. To corrupt"
"20874","(20874) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Mahak, on the authority of Hakim ibn Hizam, who said: I said: Messenger of God, a man came to me and asked me for a sale. I have nothing to sell him. Should I buy it for him in the market? He said: He said: No, do not sell what you do not have. (Tirmidhi 1233 and Abu Dawud 3497)"
"20875","(20875) Yahya bin Zakariya told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Razin, who said: I said to Masruq: A man comes to me asking me for ghee and I don’t have it to buy, then I invite him for it? He said: No, but he bought it and placed it with you, and when it comes to you, sell it from him."
"20876","(20876) Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Iyas, that Amer and Ibrahim met So they asked them about a man who asked another man for goods, but he did not have them, so he bought them, then called him to God. Abraham said: He disliked that, and Amer said: There is no problem if he wants to leave it, he can leave it."
"20877","(20877) Ibn Abi Zayd told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; About a man who wants a sale from another man who does not have it, so if they agree on the price, he will buy it? He said: He does not buy it except on the basis of what was agreed upon by its owner."
"20878","(20878) Ibn Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, that he used to hate the sale of the muradah: You describe a man with an item that you do not have, and he hates it: A man shows a man a garment that he does not have and says, “Why do you need this?” He buys it to sell it from him."
"20879","(20879) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Abi Al-Fadl, who said: I said to Al-Hasan: A man comes to me and bargains with me. With silk, which I do not have. He said: So he went to the market, then I sold it. He said: These are the specifications he thought of."
"20880","(2088) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sharik, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, who said: A man bought food from another man. Some of it is with him and some of it is not with him, so he asked Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar, and they said: He did not have it, so it is permissible, and it is not If he does not have it, then it is of nothing."
"20881","(20881) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Jadham bin Abdullah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid, On the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade buying what is in one’s stomach. Livestock until they are laid down, and whatever is in their udders except with a measure, and from buying a slave while he is lost, and from buying spoils until they are divided, And from buying alms until they are received, and from excessive strikes."
"20882","(20882) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas said: Do not sell wool for The backs of sheep, nor the milk in the udders."
"20883","(20883) Ibn al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Bishr, that he heard Ikrimah say: Do not buy deception from The stray animal, nor the lost slave, for you do not know, perhaps you will never find them, and your capital will be eaten in vain."
"20884","(20884) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of deception. (Muslim 1153. Abu Dawud 3369)q"
"20885","(20885) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Sinan bin Salamah, that a man bought a slave from another man. He returned the sale."
"20886","(20886) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: No. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the sale of deception. (Ahmad 144. Ibn Hibban 4972)"
"20887","(2088) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade And peace be upon him, regarding the sale of deception."
"20888","(20888) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to hate selling Gharar"
"20889","(20889) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin and Al-Sha’bi, who said: It is not permissible to sell it until The seller knows what the buyer knows."
"20890","(20890) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: A man came to Sharih and said: I have a servant who has returned, and he is a man. He bargains with me for it, so I will sell it to him? He said: Yes, if you see it, you have a choice. If you wish, you may accept the sale, but if you wish, you may not accept it."
"20891","(20891) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: If he informs him of it what he knew of it, it is permissible to sell it and not He has a choice."
"20892","(20892) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a man who bought an escaped slave and found him, or did not find him. He thought about it and said: It is deception."
"20893","(20893) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: I do not know of any harm in selling deception."
"20894","(20894) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ubad Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar that he bought a camel And he is distracted."
"20895","(20895) Abu Saad told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that he did not see any harm in A man buys an absent animal if he has seen it and says: If it is true, then it is mine."
"20896","(20896) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, that the people said: I wish we had We saw a sale between Abd al-Rahman bin Awf and Uthman, in order to see which of them was the greatest in trade, so he bought. Abd al-Rahman from Uthman for forty thousand mares, and he made a stipulation that if the race was to be overtaken while he was alive I brought it to the shepherd, but it was not a stray, so it was necessary to sell it. Then he passed something, and Abdul Rahman said: What have you done? Then he came back to him and said: I will give you six thousand more than if the Messenger reaches it while he is alive, then I will do so. So the Messenger reaches it while he is still alive. She spent, so Abdul Rahman was released from the guarantee according to the other condition."
"20897","(20897) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, that he saw no harm in In the sale of deception if their knowledge of it is equal."
"20898","(20898) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade About the deceived sale.\n(Abdul Razzaq 14507)"
"20899","(20899) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the sale of deception."
"20900","(20900) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I asked Ata’: Did Ibn Umar have intercourse with his housemaid? He said: Yes, and Ibn Abbas."
"20901","(20901) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of al-Sha’abi, he said: If a man plots His kingdom, he has the right to enter it."
"20902","(20902) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: He may have intercourse with her."
"20903","(20903) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not think there was anything wrong with a man stepping foot in his house."
"20904","(20904) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’ and Tawus: They did not see any harm in having intercourse with a freed man. Back"
"20905","(20905) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin that they did not see any harm in A man frees his female slave after a while, then he has sexual intercourse with her."
"20906","(20906) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: There is no harm for a man to enjoy his companionship."
"20907","(20907) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no harm in him having sexual intercourse with her."
"20908","(20908) Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of al-Zuhri, that he disliked that A man deceives his female slave and has freed her from the past."
"20909","(20909) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, and Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Hakim, he said: I asked Salim bin Abdullah, is the man who has intercourse with his wife? He said: I have her now."
"20910","(20910) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Asama bin Zaid, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: If a man dies And he must dowry his wife, which is the worst of fines. If there is oil, wheat, or anything else in his house, It is for the heirs, unless it is a name for the one with which he entered into marriage, and this is valid."
"20911","(20911) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Sawadah bin Ziyad and Amr bin Muhajir, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote To those who are guardians of religion and women’s dowries, they are the worst of debtors."
"20912","(20912) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, regarding a group of people who are all written together and some of them die. He said: The rest are striving to do what they were all prescribed for."
"20913","(20913) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, he said: I asked Omar: What Al-Hasan used to say; Concerning a man who wrote down all his kingdoms and some of them died. He said: He will remove from them the gravestone."
"20914","(20914) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, about a man who wrote down two of his slaves, and one of them died. He said: It is raised. He cursed him with the stone."
"20915","(20915) Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ghaniyya, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Concerning a man who writes all of the Ahl al-Bayt and some of them die. He said: He will be taken away with the pebbles."
"20916","(20916) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ali, about a man who bought a slave girl and she gave birth to him. Children, then the man established the clear evidence that she is his. He said: She will be returned to him, and her children will be appointed against him, and the one who sold her will be fined for what Glory be to Him."
"20917","(20917) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, about a man who found his female slave with a man who had bought her, and she had given birth. From him, he said: He takes it and takes the value of the child from their father and collects from them something of the value."
"20918","(20918) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Abu Misra said: The place of every servant is a servant. An obligatory duty that they had milked and sacrificed."
"20919","(20919) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The place of every servant is a servant."
"20920","(20920) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I said to him: When will the child be raised? He said: The day they were born."
"20921","(20921) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, who said: Ibn Abbas may include the naked woman if her owner wishes."
"20922","(20922) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Sawada bin Ziyad, who said: I wrote to Omar bin Abdul Aziz about A woman borrowed jewelry for a wedding and the jewelry was lost. Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: There is no guarantee on her unless it is unexpected. Unbelievably"
"20923","(20923) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Omar bin Abd al-Aziz, that he used to guarantee the naked person."
"20924","(20924) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, that Ali said in Al-‘Aariyah: He is trustworthy."
"20925","(20925) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Shabak, he said: A woman borrowed her rings and wanted to perform ablution. So she put it in her lap and it was lost, so they went up to Shurayh, and he said: She was only borrowed to return it, but she disagreed, so Shurayh included it."
"20926","(20926) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The one who reclaims and the borrower has no guarantee except that They disagree with us."
"20927","(20927) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyya told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad that they They did not guarantee the borrower."
"20928","(20928) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If the owner of a naked thing violates his obligation, he is liable."
"20929","(20929) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The naked person is guaranteed."
"20930","(20930) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, and Muhammad bin Sharik, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, that Ibn Abbas was The naked woman is guaranteed, and Ibn Juraij added: If her owner follows her."
"20931","(20931) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Saleh, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Muhammad bin al-Hanafiyyah, on the authority of Ali, who said: The loan is not a sale, nor is it guaranteed. Rather, it is known unless it is different and is guaranteed."
"20932","(20932) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, about a man who borrowed a horse from a man and galloped it until it died. He said: He has no liability because the man is riding his horse."
"20933","(20933) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, that it was He includes the naked woman."
"20934","(20934) Ibn Abi Za’idah told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he borrows an animal, he drives it into his own hands."
"20935","(20935) Jarir told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of people from the family of Abdullah bin Safwan, that Safwan escaped. From the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent to him, and he believed him and gave him peace, and he was the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wanted Hunayn and said: O Safwan, do you have any weapons? He said: naked or by force? He said: No, but I will loan him, so he lent him between thirty and forty shields, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, attacked. Hanan, when he defeated the polytheists, Safwan’s shields were gathered, and some of them were missing, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Safwan, we have lost some of your armor, so shall we fine you? He said: No, O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, there is in my heart today what was not there. (Abu Dawud 3558. Ahmad 3/401)"
"20936","(20936) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: No one has ever embraced a naked woman except a woman. She borrowed a ring and put it in her sink, so she unzipped it and we took it in."
"20937","(20937) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Ash-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of Shurayh, that he used to guarantee The naked one"
"20938","(20938) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: It was a share that did not guarantee the naked. And he was gentle until Ziyad commanded him, saying: So I said to him: How did he do that? He said: He continued to guarantee it until he died."
"20939","(20939) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Sa’ib, that a man borrowed a camel from another man and it became damaged. The camel, so Marwan asked Abu Hurairah and he said: Yes."
"20940","(20940) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Muslim Al-Khawlani, who said: I heard Abu Umamah Al-Bailili He said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying in the Farewell Hajj: The naked will be paid, the debt will be paid, and the leader Gharim means guarantor. (Tirmidhi 1265. Abu Dawud 4560)"
"20941","(20941) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: As long as you take it until you pay it back. (Abu Dawud 3556. Ahmad 8)"
"20942","(20942) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The mukatab is a slave who does not remain in charge. Dirham"
"20943","(20943) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The mukatab is a slave as long as he remains. He must write a dirham."
"20944","(20944) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, On the authority of Zaid, he said: He said: The mukatab is a slave who does not owe a dirham."
"20945","(20945) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ma’bad Al-Jahni, on the authority of Omar, who said: The mukatab is a slave who does not have a dirham left on him."
"20946","(20946) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of a man, who said: Omar said: A mukatab is a slave who does not remain in charge. Dirham"
"20947","(20947) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, who said: I asked permission to come to Aisha. She said: Solomon? So I said: Suleiman. She said: You have fulfilled what remained of your writing that you boycotted from your family. I said: Yes, except for something. Easy. She said: Enter, for you are a slave and nothing remains upon you."
"20948","(20948) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Layth, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The mothers of the believers did not hide themselves from the offices. He remains owed a mithqal or a dinar from writing to him."
"20949","(20949) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far bin Burqan, on the authority of Maimun, that Aisha said to someone who was writing to her that he called her father. Maryam: Come in, even if you only have four dirhams left."
"20950","(20950) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Hadd al-mukatib The limit of the owned."
"20951","(20951) Abdid bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Salih bin Hayy, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The limit of the offices is the limit of the property as long as it remains. She has a dirham."
"20952","(20952) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zahri, who said: The mukatab is a slave who does not have a dirham left on him."
"20953","(20953) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Othman said: A mukatab is a slave who does not owe a dirham."
"20954","(20954) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Uthman, who said: The office is a slave as long as there is not a dirham left on him."
"20955","(20955) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Al-Furat, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Sayegh, on the authority of Ata’, and Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair and Nafi’ said: The mukatab is a slave who does not have a dirham left on him."
"20956","(20956) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: Abdullah said: When he fulfills the duties from I left him, but there was no response to him regarding slavery."
"20957","(20957) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, and on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’abi, who said: Abdullah said: If The clerk pays one-third of his correspondence, so he is a debtor."
"20958","(20958) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: If the person despatched pays half of what he has despatched, then he is a debtor to pay."
"20959","(20959) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa`id, on the authority of Urwah, that Marwan used to judge when The one who receives letters pays half of his letters, so it is a debt that is followed by it. I mentioned that to Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, but he refused. To take it"
"20960","(20960) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, and Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Jabir bin Samarra, who said: Omar said: You are writing in writing, but if he pays half, there is no reply to him in the letter."
"20961","(20961) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Mas’udi, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, who said: The emancipation will take place on the first day of A star"
"20962","(20962) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of al-Hasan, that he said in the offices of which he was unable, and he had fulfilled some of his offices. They made a condition on it, so is it rejected? He said: If he pays half, then he is a debtor."
"20963","(20963) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, who said: If he pays half, then he is a debtor."
"20964","(20964) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he pays a third, or a quarter, or a half It is not for them to enslave him."
"20965","(20965) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Nabhan, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: If one of you has offices and has something to deliver, then you should veil yourself from him. (Tirmidhi 1261, Abu Dawud 3924)"
"20966","(20966) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It used to be said: If he pays a third, Or a quarter, it is a debt."
"20967","(20967) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali, he said: He will be freed from the offices. As much as he did."
"20968","(20968) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Harith and his companions, and on the authority of his servants, on the authority of Abraham, who said: And the loan Immediately, even if it is for a later period."
"20969","(20969) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whoever sells his pregnant woman, or frees them and excludes what is in them, Her stomach. He said to him: It is his double in what his character has made clear, and if he does not make his character clear, then there is nothing wrong with him."
"20970","(20970) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to allow two pairs in a sale, but he did not It permits emancipation."
"20971","(20971) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad; Concerning a man who frees a slave woman and spares what is in her womb. He said to him: His two."
"20972","(20972) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: They are both Haran."
"20973","(20973) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, On the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: If he frees her and excludes what is in her belly, then it is his. His two"
"20974","(20974) Harami bin Amara bin Abi Hafsiya told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad, and they said: That. No"
"20975","(20975) Qurayh bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Fada’i, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Concerning a man who sells a slave woman and excludes what is in her stomach. He said: He has a double."
"20976","(20976) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith; Concerning a man who calls the animal in the man’s hand and says: It has gone astray. He said: I will not say to the witnesses: He was not sold and did not give away. But when the witnesses testify that his animal has strayed from him, I will swear to him by God: He has not sold it, nor has he given it as a gift."
"20977","(20977) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: When the witnesses testify, it will be a mount. I swear to God: I have not destroyed you, nor have I commanded anyone to destroy you."
"20978","(20978) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Saleh, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, on the authority of Hassan bin Thumamah, Hudhayfiya recognized a sentence of his own, so he disputed over it before a Muslim judge, and Hudhayfah became a right-hander in the judgement. So he swore by God that there is no god but Him: he did not sell it, nor did he give it away."
"20979","(20979) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, he said: Al-Hajjaj used to give people sustenance, and the owners of the house of sustenance would say: Whoever wants, he can take it. Four stalks of barley with two stalks of wheat of his own. So we asked Abraham and Al-Shu’abi and they said: There is no problem with it."
"20980","(20980) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: If the two types differ, there is no problem. Thanks, hand in hand."
"20981","(20981) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, that Ibn Umar saw no harm in It is measured hand to hand, one by two, if their colors are different."
"20982","(20982) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: If the two types differ, sell as you wish."
"20983","(20983) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that he saw no harm in selling wheat for barley. Hand in hand, one more than the other."
"20984","(20984) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Muslim bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath al-San’ani, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, said: There is no harm in selling wheat for barley, and barley for more than that, hand to hand. He is not suitable for his wife."
"20985","(20985) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Anis bin Khalid Al-Tamimi, who said: I asked Ata’ about barley with wheat. Two by one, hand to hand, and he said: There is no problem with it."
"20986","(20986) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Wheat for wheat and barley for barley, hand for hand, measure for measure, weight for weight, there is no problem, so whoever adds or It has increased, so it has grown in size, except that its colors are different. (Muslim 84. Ahmad 2/262)"
"20987","(20987) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath Al-San’ani, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Gold for gold, silver for silver, righteousness for righteousness. And barley for barley, like for like, hand to hand. If these types differ, then sell as you wish, if it is hand to hand. With your hand\n(Muslim 81. Abu Dawud 3343)"
"20988","(20988) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, that Omar He sent a servant of his, or a slave of his, with a saa of dates to buy for himself a saa of barley, and he rebuked him if they increased his duty."
"20989","(20989) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, that he used to hate it. A leap of wheat with two leaps of barley."
"20990","(20990) Shababih narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Aswad bin Abd Ghuth al-Zuhri: His servant came to him and was told that his barley had died, so he ordered him to take some of his wheat. So he buys barley for him, and he does not take it except like for like. Nafi’ said: And Suleiman bin Yassar informed me. Likewise, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas."
"20991","(20991) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by A man was selling food that had barley in it, so he said: Isolate this one from that one, and this one from that one, then sell that one as a whole. Whatever you wish, sell it however you wish, for there is no deception in our religion. (Abu Dawud 174)"
"20992","(20992) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Yaman Abi Hudhayf, on the authority of Ziyad Mawla Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he was asked about a man who mixed barley with wheat, then sold it. He said: There is no harm in him."
"20993","(20993) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Yaman Abi Hudhayf that he asked Shu’bi about his thoughts."
"20994","(20994) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, that he hated for a man to buy good food. And the bad one, he mixes them all together, then sells them. If the one between them is close, then there is no problem."
"20995","(20995) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Hammad, who was asked about wheat mixed with barley. And righteousness is mixed with a worse thought than it."
"20996","(20996) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who marries the mother of his slave, and she bears him children. He said: They are in the same position as their mother, and they will be freed as she is freed. And they are regulated by its light, so when their master dies, they are freed."
"20997","(20997) Ali bin Musir and Ibn Abi Zaydah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi regarding the children of the mother of the child: They emancipate By freeing her and relieving her of her wrath."
"20998","(20998) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If the mother of the child marries and gives birth to her child, With her status."
"20999","(20999) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: Her children are in the same position as her."
"21000","(21000) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The son of the child’s mother is in her position."
"21001","(21001) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy, on the authority of Hout, that a man usurped a man’s mother and son. She bore him children, and Shurayh said: Her children are in the same position as her. He uses them, but does not sell them."
"21002","(21002) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The son of the child’s mother is in her position, They will free her by freeing her, and they will be rewarded with her martyrdom."
"21003","(21003) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, who said: The son of the son’s mother is in her position, they will be freed by her emancipation. Their owner will sell them if he wants."
"21004","(21004) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Riyah ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Umar ibn Abdul Aziz that he was the most delicate child. The boy's mother"
"21005","(21005) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: The son of the manager. With her status."
"21006","(21006) Ibn Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He was born The freed woman, at the end of her life, they will be freed by her bond and will be freed when she is freed."
"21007","(21007) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: The ruler was born from her."
"21008","(21008) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He used to say: The son of the freedman, on the authority of a woman in her position. They and their mother are from a third."
"21009","(21009) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Riyah ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Umar ibn Abdul Aziz that he made them In the same position as their mother."
"21010","(21010) Ali bin Musir and Ibn Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Her two sons are in the same position as her."
"21011","(21011) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Everything is born from On the day it is brought back, they will be in the same position as it is, they will be liberated by freeing it and will be freed from its wrath."
"21012","(21012) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Al-Qasim bin Muhammad was told that Omar bin Abdul Aziz, he said So, Al-Qasim said: This is my opinion, and I do not think his opinion on this matter was anything but moderate."
"21013","(21013) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The ruler was born in the same position as their mother."
"21014","(21014) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: He was born The one who is managed by her status, they will be freed by her freedom and they will be relieved of her wrath."
"21015","(21015) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, Shurayh, and Masruq with something similar."
"21016","(21016) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: The son of the ruler is in her position."
"21017","(21017) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amer, who said: If a woman gives birth to children, then her son In her status, if she is freed, they will be freed."
"21018","(21018) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’ And Peacock, and Mujahid, and Saeed bin Jubair, because they said: The ruler was born in the same position as their mother."
"21019","(21019) Abd al-Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a woman who emancipated a female slave of hers, after that, and she bore children after that: They are in the same position as their mother. If she is emancipated, they will be emancipated."
"21020","(21020) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I do not see children. The one who returns is only in the position of their mother."
"21021","(21021) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, who said: The children of the ruler are sold by their owner if he wishes."
"21022","(21022) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: The son of the manager is Ubaid."
"21023","(21023) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Amr bin Harith, that a man bought A slave girl for sixty dinars, so he paid thirty, and the seller entrusted her with the rest. He stayed for a few days, then the buyer came. With its price, he found that it had died, so he said: Whatever the seller took is his, and the rest is for the buyer."
"21024","(21024) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Thaqafi, that Shurayh said about her: The seller does not return the price he took and buries his corpse."
"21025","(21025) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that the statement of Amr ibn Harith was something that impressed him."
"21026","(21026) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, about a man who bought from a man. A slave girl, and he paid some of her money, and the seller seized her with the rest, and she died. He said: The buyer will be returned to him what he took. It is from the seller's money."
"21027","(21027) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: If he paid some of the price and entrusted the goods With the remainder, then the property is destroyed, so it is for what he pledged to him and what he had taken, so if it was a sale of what was measured and weighed The shortfall is on the seller until the buyer pays it."
"21028","(21028) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid who said: If the slanderer repents, it is permissible. Your testimony"
"21029","(21029) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: If he repents, and nothing is known from him except good, then his testimony is valid."
"21030","(21030) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: It is permissible His testimony when he repents."
"21031","(21031) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: His testimony is permissible if he repents."
"21032","(21032) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, I think it is, on the authority of Sa’id, who said: Omar said to Abu Bakra: If he repents, accept. Your testimony"
"21033","(21033) Ibn Idris and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Imran bin Umair, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utba, who said: It is permissible If he repents"
"21034","(21034) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: It is permissible if he repents."
"21035","(21035) Muhammad bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Al-Awwam, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, who said: It is permissible if he repents."
"21036","(21036) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: It is permissible, and he said: May God accept your repentance, but I will not allow it. Your testimony"
"21037","(21037) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: If the punishment is imposed on a man in His slander will never be accepted as evidence, and his repentance is between him and God."
"21038","(21038) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: It is not permissible to perform shahada. The slanderer, and his repentance is between him and God."
"21039","(21039) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, who said: I heard Ibrahim and Al-Shu’bi discussing That is why Ibrahim said: It is not permissible. Al-Sha’bi said: Why? Then Abraham said: You do not know whether he repented or not."
"21040","(21040) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan, that he used to say about al-Qadhif: His repentance is among them. And God made it clear, and his testimony is not permissible."
"21041","(21041) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of al-Hasan, and Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, They said: There is no witness for him, and his repentance is between him and God."
"21042","(21042) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Muslims are just to one another, except limited in their fury."
